{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179467526,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f908d1a4001eb8IxtziovDD1F","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f908ca9b001TfBxqsKGltV1W2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3ed1965211f5193","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/deep-research-config.json"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/deep-research-config.json, lines 1-136\n1: {\n2:   \"topic\": \"What changes would make the deep-loop fan-out orchestration trustworthy and identical across CLI runtimes, ranked by value over effort, given what the last two expansive dogfood runs taught?\\n\\nRead the code at HEAD b8003a7df42. The spec folder is specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode (SPEC below). Inputs: SPEC/scratch/dogfood-review-gen2.md and SPEC/scratch/dogfood-research-gen3.md (the conductor logs of the previous fan-out review and research), and the previous research with its improvement-backlog.md, now the newest folder under SPEC/research_archive/. Commits adade6c293e..07cf5f92b61 built backlog rows 1-11, 14, 16b, 18a and 19-26: build on them and do not re-report them. Every recommendation names one concrete change, cites file:line (or a source URL for prior art), and states value, effort (S/M/L) and risk.\\n\\nQ1 Lineage honesty: one lineage wrote 9 of 12 review passes 20-60 s apart, most with zero findings, and reported newInfoRatio 1.0 on all 10 research passes; model-written timestamps were placeholders, whole minutes or future-dated. Which runner-side signals (pass duration, cited locations, tool calls, repeated sources, gateway receipt time) would detect an unexamined pass or a false stamp without trusting the model, and how should convergence and fanout-merge.cjs weigh such a pass?\\n\\nQ2 Cross-CLI execution contract: across native, cli-claude-code, cli-opencode, cli-codex, cli-pi, cli-devin, cli-cursor, cli-deepseek-harness and cli-mistral-vibe, where do permission and sandbox, effort, output format (cli-claude-code still uses --output-format text, so it reports no tokens or cost), session resume, failure classes, log shape and prompt channel still differ in fanout-run.cjs LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts and dispatch-iteration.cjs (runClaude, runCodex)? What single adapter contract and conformance test would remove the differences, including the agent and co... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3:   \"maxIterations\": 10,\n4:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n5:   \"antiConvergence\": {\n6:     \"minIterations\": 3,\n7:     \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n8:     \"depthMode\": \"expansive\",\n9:     \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\",\n10:     \"divergent\": {}\n11:   },\n12:   \"expansiveDepth\": {\n13:     \"maxDepth\": 3,\n14:     \"maxChildrenPerNode\": 6,\n15:     \"budgetSplit\": {\n16:       \"depth1\": 0.5,\n17:       \"depth2\": 0.35,\n18:       \"depth3\": 0.15\n19:     },\n20:     \"maxFrontierNodes\": null\n21:   },\n22:   \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n23:   \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n24:   \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n25:   \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n26:   \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n27:   \"specFolder\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode\",\n28:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-20T12:56:45.419Z\",\n29:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n30:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n31:   \"executor\": {\n32:     \"kind\": \"native\",\n33:     \"model\": null,\n34:     \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n35:     \"serviceTier\": null,\n36:     \"sandboxMode\": null,\n37:     \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n38:   },\n39:   \"lineage\": {\n40:     \"sessionId\": \"2026-11-20T12:56:45.419Z\",\n41:     \"parentSessionId\": \"2026-11-20T01:19:42.000Z\",\n42:     \"lineageMode\": \"restart\",\n43:     \"allowedModes\": [\n44:       \"new\",\n45:       \"resume\",\n46:       \"restart\",\n47:       \"completed-continue\"\n48:     ],\n49:     \"deferredModes\": [\n50:       \"fork\"\n51:     ],\n52:     \"generation\": 4,\n53:     \"continuedFromRun\": null\n54:   },\n55:   \"reducer\": {\n56:     \"enabled\": true,\n57:     \"version\": \"1.0\",\n58:     \"registryFile\": \"research/findings-registry.json\",\n59:     \"dashboardFile\": \"research/deep-research-dashboard.md\",\n60:     \"strategyFile\": \"research/deep-research-strategy.md\",\n61:     \"machineOwnedSections\": [\n62:       \"key-questions\",\n63:       \"answered-questions\",\n64:       \"what-worked\",\n65:       \"what-failed\",\n66:       \"exhausted-approaches\",\n67:       \"ruled-out-directions\",\n68:       \"divergence-frontier\",\n69:       \"next-focus\"\n70:     ]\n71:   },\n72:   \"capabilityMatrixPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json\",\n73:   \"capabilityMatrixDocPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md\",\n74:   \"runtimeCapabilityResolver\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs\",\n75:   \"reducerScriptPath\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs\",\n76:   \"pauseSentinelPath\": \"research/.deep-research-pause\",\n77:   \"archiveRoot\": \"research_archive\",\n78:   \"migrationWindowDays\": 28,\n79:   \"fileProtection\": {\n80:     \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n81:     \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n82:     \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n83:     \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n84:     \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n85:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n86:     \"research/research.md\": \"mutable\"\n87:   },\n88:   \"_optimizerManaged\": {\n89:     \"