{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179510752,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f9097bd8001DhuXuJYsqM0g41","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f90975900018GJgXtON9dcD6w","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-956dccc4a266866e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md, lines 1-65\n1: # Improvement Backlog: expansive-depth deep loops\n2: \n3: This backlog is ranked by value over effort. It is built from generation 3 of this packet's\n4: research (`research.md`, lineages `opus` and `deepseek`) and from the conductor's dogfood\n5: observations of the same run.\n6: \n7: Report only: nothing here has been fixed. The operator picks items.\n8: \n9: ## How to read it\n10: \n11: - **Value and Risk** are H, M or L, with M-H in between.\n12: - **Effort** is S (under a day), M (one to three days) or L (longer).\n13: - **Check** applies to the top ten. The conductor re-read the cited code at `d4420e9510d`:\n14:   - **CONFIRMED** means the code at those lines shows the mechanism, and where noted the run showed\n15:     the effect live.\n16:   - **PLAUSIBLE** means the code is consistent with the claim, but the effect was traced, not\n17:     reproduced.\n18:   - Items 11 and below carry the lineages' evidence, unchecked by the conductor.\n19: - **Rec** is do, defer or drop.\n20: - **Paths are shortened.** A `runtime/` path is under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/`, and the\n21:   two YAMLs are under `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/`.\n22: \n23: ## Top ten\n24: \n25: | # | What | Why, with evidence | Value | Effort | Risk | Check | Rec |\n26: |---|------|--------------------|-------|--------|------|-------|-----|\n27: | 1 | Append `{reducer_artifact_arg}` to the single-loop `step_emit_resource_map` command | The `if_absent` command at `deep-research.yaml:2155` has no `--artifact-dir`. A fan-out lineage therefore resolves the root config and fails with ENOENT. The deepseek lineage hit it (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:190`), and opus worked around it (`lineages/opus/research.md:99`). The binding already exists (`deep-research.yaml:268-276`). | H | S | L | CONFIRMED, live in both lineages | do |\n28: | 2 | Resolve the Claude permission mode in the single-executor review dispatcher, as research does | `dispatch-iteration.cjs:379` hardcodes `--permission-mode acceptEdits` on the review branch, while the research branch calls `resolveClaudePermissionMode` (`:424`). The review leaf must run `append-mode-event.cjs` through `node` every iteration (`deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:109`, `:150`), but in `-p` mode `acceptEdits` cannot run Bash. A single-executor review on cli-claude-code therefore cannot record state, and `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` has no effect there (the review executor sets `sandboxMode: null`). No test pins the value. The previous dogfood probe showed the refusal with exit 0. | H | S | L | CONFIRMED (code and leaf contract; effect from the earlier probe) | do |\n29: | 3 | Write a root config on the fan-out path at spawn (topic, `config.fanout`, generation + 1, parent session) | The fan-out branch jumps from `step_fanout_spawn` to synthesis and never runs `step_create_config` (`deep-research.yaml:432-434`). Without a root config: (a) the root resource map fails, because `reduce-state.cjs:1816-1819` requires one; (b) `step_update_config_status` has nothing to mark; (c) a `--restart` records no new generation. In this run the root map failed until the conductor wrote the config late. 104 of 192 committed fan-out roots have neither a root config nor a resource map. The `:auto` setup's own persist (`research.md:88`) runs before `--restart` archives the packet, so it cannot be the fix as written. | H | S-M | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n30: | 4 | Feed the graph stop guards from the mandatory delta `finding` rows and `answeredQuestions`, not only the optional `graphEvents` | `latestGraphEvents` reads only `record.graphEvents` (`iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:118-125`), and the prompt pack calls that field optional (`prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:54`). Opus's stop was blocked by `source_diversity_guard`, `evidence_depth_guard` and `uncovered_questions` with every node answered, which cost one recovery iteration (`lineages/opus/iterations/iteration-005.md`). | H | S-M | L | CONFIRMED (code; one live occurrence) | do |\n31: | 5 | Add a per-lineage `{label, status, failure_class, exit_code, rerun_command}` array to `orchestration-summary.json` and the stdout summary | The summary keys are counts, gauges and `failure_classes` only: `run_id` ... `failure_classes`, with no lineage label (`research/orchestration-summary.json`). The pool already computes per-lineage results (`fanout-pool.cjs:977`). | H | S | L | CONFIRMED | do |\n32: | 6 | Count research stuck passes per frontier node: publish `activeNodeId` in the research projection, then drop the review-only gate | `nodeScoped` requires `loopType === 'review'` (`convergence.cjs:1774-1778`). The research reducer publishes no `activeNodeId`; the review reducer does, at `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2026`. The research stuck branch instead closes the node its own focus regex names (`deep-research.yaml:1520-1532`), so under breadth-first rotation clean passes on other nodes can close it. | M-H | S | L | CONFIRMED (mechanism; no stuck event fired in this run) | do |\n33: | 7 | Stop a fan-out lineage when its frontier drains, instead of falling back to topic questions that other lineages own | `resolveNextFocus` returns a frontier focus only while a node is open (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2571-2575`). It then falls back to the leaf and continuity focus, which comes from the full topic. Deepseek spent iterations 8-10 on Q1, Q5 and Q6, all of them opus's nodes (`lineages/deepseek/deep-research-state.jsonl`). `frontier_partition_guard` still passed, because it checks node ids only. | M | S | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n34: | 8 | Skip the settle-time metadata refresh for a research fan-out too, as review now does, or fix the description extractor | `metadataRefreshRequested` exempts review only (`fanout-run.cjs:3666-3668`). In this run it rewrote `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` outside `research/`. It replaced the curated description with an auto-extracted sentence, added stop-word keywords (\"three\", \"five\", \"init\"), and dropped the `frontier veto` and `depth-mode expansive` trigger phrases (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/metadata-refresh.diff`). | M | S | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n35: | 9 | Publish `sandboxEnforcement` (preventive, compensating or none) and `effortApplied` (flag, baked or none) in `effective_config`, and make `permissionMode` print each kind's real flag value, or null for a kind with none | The preview printed `permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\"` for the opencode lineage (`fanout-run.cjs:2486`, `:2515`). That is the Claude resolution passed through, although opencode has no permission flag. Claude (`:2582`), Devin (`auto` or `dangerous`, `:3026-3030`) and dsh (`read-only` or `workspace-write`, `:3316`) each pass their own `--permission-mode`. The truth is already tabled as `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` (`executor-config.ts:159-170`) but is not printed, so the preview cannot say what a kind actually enforces. | M | S | L | CONFIRMED (code and live preview) | do |\n36: | 10 | Make fan-out re-entrant: a pre-spawn classifier skips a lineage whose config is `complete` and whose artifacts pass `completionFromArtifacts`, plus a documented `--only-lineage=LABEL` rerun that replaces the internal `--allow-single-lineage` | `readStoredLineageSessionId` returns null for a complete config (`fanout-run.cjs:770-778`), so a re-dispatched finished lineage gets a new session. It then halts at `completed-session` without a terminal row and fails `stale_terminal_event`. The previous run's single-lineage recovery needed a hand-edited matrix. This mirrors Inspect `eval_set` (https://inspect.aisi.org.uk/eval-sets.html). It also answers open question 5b. | H | M | M | PLAUSIBLE (code read; re-dispatch not reproduced) | do |\n37: \n38: ## The rest, ranked\n39: \n40: | # | What | Why, with evidence | Value | Effort | Risk | Rec |\n41: |---|------|--------------------|-------|--------|------|-----|\n42: | 11 | Move the 15 inline `node -e` programs out of the two YAMLs into one runtime script | Every CLI lineage transcribes them, and they are the main cross-runtime variance (`deep-research.yaml:534-630`, `:858-905`; 8 in review) [opus] | H | M | L | do |\n43: | 12 | Replace the two reducer frontier projections with one `projectFrontier` in `frontier-admit.cjs`, and keep one node-marker parser | `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2453-2534`, `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1960-2030`, and the marker parsers at `convergence.cjs:1359-1395` and `frontier-admit.cjs:1014` [opus, deepseek] | H | M | M (206 frontier test assertions) | do, after 6 |\n44: | 13 | Collapse the six single-executor YAML executor branches into one, routed through `buildLineageCommand`, and delete the hand-built `runClaude` and `runCodex` | `deep-research.yaml:1762-1837` and review's twin; about 300 runtime lines and 100 lines per YAML. It subsumes item 2 [deepseek] | H | M | M | do, after 2 |\n45: | 14 | Write answered and budget closes into the node store, or label the store as lifecycle-only | After the run every seed reads `open` in `lineages/*/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, while the projection says answered or exhausted. The only research store close is the stuck close (`deep-research.yaml:1528`) [conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n46: | 15 | Tolerant pre-spawn completion rule and strict post-attempt rule (the 5b answer) | 98 of 380 committed research lineage logs fail the live rule retroactively, 84 of them with a `research.md` (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/completion-check.txt`) [all three] | M | S | L | do, with 10 |\n47: | 16 | Fund the frontier from its nodes: reserve growth slots, and tell the run cap apart from the per-parent cap in the prune reason | The node cap of 5 filled at iteration 1 and pruned 5 of deepseek's 7 proposals as `fanout`. The reason name is shared by both caps (`frontier-admit.cjs:774-781`). The derived budget is a constant 10 for any 2-lineage research run (`frontier-admit.cjs:469-476`) [deepseek, conductor] | M-H | S-M | M | do |\n48: | 17 | Admit an accepted pivot as a synthetic depth-2 `frontier_proposal` under the last-worked node, falling back to D-011-10 when it is pruned (the 5c answer) | It answers D-011-10's three reasons with inherited scope, band carry and the `frontierOpen` veto (`011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68`). It needs a reserved slot (item 16) [opus, deepseek] | M | S-M | M | defer, until 16 lands |\n49: | 18 | Sum provider cost from JSON lineage logs into the attribution and summary, and switch cli-claude-code to `--output-format json` or `stream-json` so cost is captured | Deepseek's log sums to $0.326, but the runner never reads it. Opus's text log carries no tokens or cost. \"Cost units\" count iterations only (`fanout-run.cjs:1386-1407`) [conductor, opus] | M | S-M | L | do |\n50: | 19 | Merge the duplicate question intake: legacy key questions and frontier questions | 3 of 11 questions stayed open after their frontier twins were answered (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:187`) [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n51: | 20 | Validate Next Focus so it is always a question | Next Focus became \"Close F-2-008 as answered ...\" (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:100`) [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n52: | 21 | Replace the 486-word `--depth-mode` cell in `research.md:107` with a pointer, as `review.md` already does | It duplicates the presentation table and the loop protocol [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n53: | 22 | Fix stale examples in `deep-research-presentation.txt` | The fan-out examples use an empty `--label=` and `claude-opus-4-8` (`:391-403`). The Q-Exec B line documents the v1 opencode flags `--variant`, `--dangerously-skip-permissions` and `--pure`, while v2 builds `-m model#effort --auto` (`:194`) [conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n54: | 23 | Replace the stale \"seven to eight minutes an iteration\" estimate with measured ranges | `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464`. This run measured 0.5 to 5 min, and the committed reviews 1.5 to 3.7 min [deepseek, conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n55: | 24 | Rename the \"FATAL WARN\" banner for opencode `--auto` to a plain warning | It prints on every opencode lineage and is not fatal (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/preview.err`) [conductor] | L-M | S | L | do |\n56: | 25 | Make the dry run's `dry_run_halt` line come from a script, and print the topic digest beside the prompt digest | The halt line is conductor-emitted prose (`deep-research.yaml:107`), and the preview cannot confirm the topic [conductor] | L-M | S | L | do |\n57: | 26 | Label `aggregate_budget` units in the preview | The aggregate `estimated_cost_units` reads 20 while each lineage's reads 60 (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/preview.out`) [conductor] | L | S | L | do |\n58: | 27 | Spell the research archive folder like review's, or document both | Research uses `research_archive/` and review uses `review-archive/` (`review-research-paths.cjs`) [conductor] | L | S | M (moves existing archives) | defer |\n59: | 28 | Repetition-based stuck signal, in the style of OpenHands' stuck detector | Deepseek's self-reported ratio was 1.0 on all 10 passes, so it could stop only on the cap. Repetition of sources and finding ids is observable, while a ratio is self-asserted (https://docs.openhands.dev/sdk/guides/agent-stuck-detector) [opus] | M | S | M | defer: in this run the passes were real work, so repetition would not have fired |\n60: | 29 | Delete the 24 config-key aliases, the expired legacy-name migration, the 8 binary probes, the 19 `bookkeeping_log` templates and the `append-mode-event.cjs` cwd fallbacks | `fanout-run.cjs:1374-1407`, `:3582-3647`; `deep-research.yaml:175-180`, `:489-504`, `:2202` [opus, deepseek] | M | S | L-M | do, in one restraint pass |\n61: | 30 | Per-node visits in the research dashboard, and one shared frontier dashboard renderer | Review computes visits (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1972`); research drops them [deepseek] | M | S-M | L | do, with 12 |\n62: | 31 | Effort-scaling table and a pre-spawn cost estimate in both command docs | Anthropic's multi-agent research system and LangChain open_deep_research (URLs in `research.md` section 10) [deepseek] | M | S | L | defer, until 18 gives real cost data |\n63: | 32 | Derive `maxDurationMinutes` from the iteration cap | The measured iteration times put 24 iterations at 12 to 120 minutes, inside the 120-minute default. The premise of an 8 to 11 minute iteration did not reproduce [deepseek] | L | S | L | drop |\n64: | 33 | Skip the context ladder in fan-out children | Measured setup to config was 1.3 to 1.7 min in this run, not 3 to 10 [deepseek] | L | M | M | drop |\n65: | 34 | Geometric child cap in place of band-budget closes | GPT Researcher's breadth halving (`research.md` section 10) [opus] | M | M | M | defer, evaluate after 16 |","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md, lines 1-65\n1: # Improvement Backlog: expansive-depth deep loops\n2: \n3: This backlog is ranked by value over effort. It is built from generation 3 of this packet's\n4: research (`research.md`, lineages `opus` and `deepseek`) and from the conductor's dogfood\n5: observations of the same run.\n6: \n7: Report only: nothing here has been fixed. The operator picks items.\n8: \n9: ## How to read it\n10: \n11: - **Value and Risk** are H, M or L, with M-H in between.\n12: - **Effort** is S (under a day), M (one to three days) or L (longer).\n13: - **Check** applies to the top ten. The conductor re-read the cited code at `d4420e9510d`:\n14:   - **CONFIRMED** means the code at those lines shows the mechanism, and where noted the run showed\n15:     the effect live.\n16:   - **PLAUSIBLE** means the code is consistent with the claim, but the effect was traced, not\n17:     reproduced.\n18:   - Items 11 and below carry the lineages' evidence, unchecked by the conductor.\n19: - **Rec** is do, defer or drop.\n20: - **Paths are shortened.** A `runtime/` path is under `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/`, and the\n21:   two YAMLs are under `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/`.\n22: \n23: ## Top ten\n24: \n25: | # | What | Why, with evidence | Value | Effort | Risk | Check | Rec |\n26: |---|------|--------------------|-------|--------|------|-------|-----|\n27: | 1 | Append `{reducer_artifact_arg}` to the single-loop `step_emit_resource_map` command | The `if_absent` command at `deep-research.yaml:2155` has no `--artifact-dir`. A fan-out lineage therefore resolves the root config and fails with ENOENT. The deepseek lineage hit it (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:190`), and opus worked around it (`lineages/opus/research.md:99`). The binding already exists (`deep-research.yaml:268-276`). | H | S | L | CONFIRMED, live in both lineages | do |\n28: | 2 | Resolve the Claude permission mode in the single-executor review dispatcher, as research does | `dispatch-iteration.cjs:379` hardcodes `--permission-mode acceptEdits` on the review branch, while the research branch calls `resolveClaudePermissionMode` (`:424`). The review leaf must run `append-mode-event.cjs` through `node` every iteration (`deep-review/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:109`, `:150`), but in `-p` mode `acceptEdits` cannot run Bash. A single-executor review on cli-claude-code therefore cannot record state, and `--sandbox-mode=danger-full-access` has no effect there (the review executor sets `sandboxMode: null`). No test pins the value. The previous dogfood probe showed the refusal with exit 0. | H | S | L | CONFIRMED (code and leaf contract; effect from the earlier probe) | do |\n29: | 3 | Write a root config on the fan-out path at spawn (topic, `config.fanout`, generation + 1, parent session) | The fan-out branch jumps from `step_fanout_spawn` to synthesis and never runs `step_create_config` (`deep-research.yaml:432-434`). Without a root config: (a) the root resource map fails, because `reduce-state.cjs:1816-1819` requires one; (b) `step_update_config_status` has nothing to mark; (c) a `--restart` records no new generation. In this run the root map failed until the conductor wrote the config late. 104 of 192 committed fan-out roots have neither a root config nor a resource map. The `:auto` setup's own persist (`research.md:88`) runs before `--restart` archives the packet, so it cannot be the fix as written. | H | S-M | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n30: | 4 | Feed the graph stop guards from the mandatory delta `finding` rows and `answeredQuestions`, not only the optional `graphEvents` | `latestGraphEvents` reads only `record.graphEvents` (`iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:118-125`), and the prompt pack calls that field optional (`prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl:54`). Opus's stop was blocked by `source_diversity_guard`, `evidence_depth_guard` and `uncovered_questions` with every node answered, which cost one recovery iteration (`lineages/opus/iterations/iteration-005.md`). | H | S-M | L | CONFIRMED (code; one live occurrence) | do |\n31: | 5 | Add a per-lineage `{label, status, failure_class, exit_code, rerun_command}` array to `orchestration-summary.json` and the stdout summary | The summary keys are counts, gauges and `failure_classes` only: `run_id` ... `failure_classes`, with no lineage label (`research/orchestration-summary.json`). The pool already computes per-lineage results (`fanout-pool.cjs:977`). | H | S | L | CONFIRMED | do |\n32: | 6 | Count research stuck passes per frontier node: publish `activeNodeId` in the research projection, then drop the review-only gate | `nodeScoped` requires `loopType === 'review'` (`convergence.cjs:1774-1778`). The research reducer publishes no `activeNodeId`; the review reducer does, at `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2026`. The research stuck branch instead closes the node its own focus regex names (`deep-research.yaml:1520-1532`), so under breadth-first rotation clean passes on other nodes can close it. | M-H | S | L | CONFIRMED (mechanism; no stuck event fired in this run) | do |\n33: | 7 | Stop a fan-out lineage when its frontier drains, instead of falling back to topic questions that other lineages own | `resolveNextFocus` returns a frontier focus only while a node is open (`deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2571-2575`). It then falls back to the leaf and continuity focus, which comes from the full topic. Deepseek spent iterations 8-10 on Q1, Q5 and Q6, all of them opus's nodes (`lineages/deepseek/deep-research-state.jsonl`). `frontier_partition_guard` still passed, because it checks node ids only. | M | S | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n34: | 8 | Skip the settle-time metadata refresh for a research fan-out too, as review now does, or fix the description extractor | `metadataRefreshRequested` exempts review only (`fanout-run.cjs:3666-3668`). In this run it rewrote `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` outside `research/`. It replaced the curated description with an auto-extracted sentence, added stop-word keywords (\"three\", \"five\", \"init\"), and dropped the `frontier veto` and `depth-mode expansive` trigger phrases (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/metadata-refresh.diff`). | M | S | L | CONFIRMED, live | do |\n35: | 9 | Publish `sandboxEnforcement` (preventive, compensating or none) and `effortApplied` (flag, baked or none) in `effective_config`, and make `permissionMode` print each kind's real flag value, or null for a kind with none | The preview printed `permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\"` for the opencode lineage (`fanout-run.cjs:2486`, `:2515`). That is the Claude resolution passed through, although opencode has no permission flag. Claude (`:2582`), Devin (`auto` or `dangerous`, `:3026-3030`) and dsh (`read-only` or `workspace-write`, `:3316`) each pass their own `--permission-mode`. The truth is already tabled as `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY` (`executor-config.ts:159-170`) but is not printed, so the preview cannot say what a kind actually enforces. | M | S | L | CONFIRMED (code and live preview) | do |\n36: | 10 | Make fan-out re-entrant: a pre-spawn classifier skips a lineage whose config is `complete` and whose artifacts pass `completionFromArtifacts`, plus a documented `--only-lineage=LABEL` rerun that replaces the internal `--allow-single-lineage` | `readStoredLineageSessionId` returns null for a complete config (`fanout-run.cjs:770-778`), so a re-dispatched finished lineage gets a new session. It then halts at `completed-session` without a terminal row and fails `stale_terminal_event`. The previous run's single-lineage recovery needed a hand-edited matrix. This mirrors Inspect `eval_set` (https://inspect.aisi.org.uk/eval-sets.html). It also answers open question 5b. | H | M | M | PLAUSIBLE (code read; re-dispatch not reproduced) | do |\n37: \n38: ## The rest, ranked\n39: \n40: | # | What | Why, with evidence | Value | Effort | Risk | Rec |\n41: |---|------|--------------------|-------|--------|------|-----|\n42: | 11 | Move the 15 inline `node -e` programs out of the two YAMLs into one runtime script | Every CLI lineage transcribes them, and they are the main cross-runtime variance (`deep-research.yaml:534-630`, `:858-905`; 8 in review) [opus] | H | M | L | do |\n43: | 12 | Replace the two reducer frontier projections with one `projectFrontier` in `frontier-admit.cjs`, and keep one node-marker parser | `deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:2453-2534`, `runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1960-2030`, and the marker parsers at `convergence.cjs:1359-1395` and `frontier-admit.cjs:1014` [opus, deepseek] | H | M | M (206 frontier test assertions) | do, after 6 |\n44: | 13 | Collapse the six single-executor YAML executor branches into one, routed through `buildLineageCommand`, and delete the hand-built `runClaude` and `runCodex` | `deep-research.yaml:1762-1837` and review's twin; about 300 runtime lines and 100 lines per YAML. It subsumes item 2 [deepseek] | H | M | M | do, after 2 |\n45: | 14 | Write answered and budget closes into the node store, or label the store as lifecycle-only | After the run every seed reads `open` in `lineages/*/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, while the projection says answered or exhausted. The only research store close is the stuck close (`deep-research.yaml:1528`) [conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n46: | 15 | Tolerant pre-spawn completion rule and strict post-attempt rule (the 5b answer) | 98 of 380 committed research lineage logs fail the live rule retroactively, 84 of them with a `research.md` (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/completion-check.txt`) [all three] | M | S | L | do, with 10 |\n47: | 16 | Fund the frontier from its nodes: reserve growth slots, and tell the run cap apart from the per-parent cap in the prune reason | The node cap of 5 filled at iteration 1 and pruned 5 of deepseek's 7 proposals as `fanout`. The reason name is shared by both caps (`frontier-admit.cjs:774-781`). The derived budget is a constant 10 for any 2-lineage research run (`frontier-admit.cjs:469-476`) [deepseek, conductor] | M-H | S-M | M | do |\n48: | 17 | Admit an accepted pivot as a synthetic depth-2 `frontier_proposal` under the last-worked node, falling back to D-011-10 when it is pruned (the 5c answer) | It answers D-011-10's three reasons with inherited scope, band carry and the `frontierOpen` veto (`011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md:68`). It needs a reserved slot (item 16) [opus, deepseek] | M | S-M | M | defer, until 16 lands |\n49: | 18 | Sum provider cost from JSON lineage logs into the attribution and summary, and switch cli-claude-code to `--output-format json` or `stream-json` so cost is captured | Deepseek's log sums to $0.326, but the runner never reads it. Opus's text log carries no tokens or cost. \"Cost units\" count iterations only (`fanout-run.cjs:1386-1407`) [conductor, opus] | M | S-M | L | do |\n50: | 19 | Merge the duplicate question intake: legacy key questions and frontier questions | 3 of 11 questions stayed open after their frontier twins were answered (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:187`) [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n51: | 20 | Validate Next Focus so it is always a question | Next Focus became \"Close F-2-008 as answered ...\" (`lineages/deepseek/research.md:100`) [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n52: | 21 | Replace the 486-word `--depth-mode` cell in `research.md:107` with a pointer, as `review.md` already does | It duplicates the presentation table and the loop protocol [deepseek] | M | S | L | do |\n53: | 22 | Fix stale examples in `deep-research-presentation.txt` | The fan-out examples use an empty `--label=` and `claude-opus-4-8` (`:391-403`). The Q-Exec B line documents the v1 opencode flags `--variant`, `--dangerously-skip-permissions` and `--pure`, while v2 builds `-m model#effort --auto` (`:194`) [conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n54: | 23 | Replace the stale \"seven to eight minutes an iteration\" estimate with measured ranges | `deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md:464`. This run measured 0.5 to 5 min, and the committed reviews 1.5 to 3.7 min [deepseek, conductor] | M | S | L | do |\n55: | 24 | Rename the \"FATAL WARN\" banner for opencode `--auto` to a plain warning | It prints on every opencode lineage and is not fatal (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/preview.err`) [conductor] | L-M | S | L | do |\n56: | 25 | Make the dry run's `dry_run_halt` line come from a script, and print the topic digest beside the prompt digest | The halt line is conductor-emitted prose (`deep-research.yaml:107`), and the preview cannot confirm the topic [conductor] | L-M | S | L | do |\n57: | 26 | Label `aggregate_budget` units in the preview | The aggregate `estimated_cost_units` reads 20 while each lineage's reads 60 (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/preview.out`) [conductor] | L | S | L | do |\n58: | 27 | Spell the research archive folder like review's, or document both | Research uses `research_archive/` and review uses `review-archive/` (`review-research-paths.cjs`) [conductor] | L | S | M (moves existing archives) | defer |\n59: | 28 | Repetition-based stuck signal, in the style of OpenHands' stuck detector | Deepseek's self-reported ratio was 1.0 on all 10 passes, so it could stop only on the cap. Repetition of sources and finding ids is observable, while a ratio is self-asserted (https://docs.openhands.dev/sdk/guides/agent-stuck-detector) [opus] | M | S | M | defer: in this run the passes were real work, so repetition would not have fired |\n60: | 29 | Delete the 24 config-key aliases, the expired legacy-name migration, the 8 binary probes, the 19 `bookkeeping_log` templates and the `append-mode-event.cjs` cwd fallbacks | `fanout-run.cjs:1374-1407`, `:3582-3647`; `deep-research.yaml:175-180`, `:489-504`, `:2202` [opus, deepseek] | M | S | L-M | do, in one restraint pass |\n61: | 30 | Per-node visits in the research dashboard, and one shared frontier dashboard renderer | Review computes visits (`runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs:1972`); research drops them [deepseek] | M | S-M | L | do, with 12 |\n62: | 31 | Effort-scaling table and a pre-spawn cost estimate in both command docs | Anthropic's multi-agent research system and LangChain open_deep_research (URLs in `research.md` section 10) [deepseek] | M | S | L | defer, until 18 gives real cost data |\n63: | 32 | Derive `maxDurationMinutes` from the iteration cap | The measured iteration times put 24 iterations at 12 to 120 minutes, inside the 120-minute default. The premise of an 8 to 11 minute iteration did not reproduce [deepseek] | L | S | L | drop |\n64: | 33 | Skip the context ladder in fan-out children | Measured setup to config was 1.3 to 1.7 min in this run, not 3 to 10 [deepseek] | L | M | M | drop |\n65: | 34 | Geometric child cap in place of band-budget closes | GPT Researcher's breadth halving (`research.md` section 10) [opus] | M | M | M | defer, evaluate after 16 |"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795179510744,"end":1795179510752}}}}
