{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179516987,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f90993ba002ewB5yIeyRU1Dmc","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9098ee500119ZG0Z5o796uCc","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-828e9651f66719cc","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-review-gen2.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-review-gen2.md, lines 1-441\n1: # Dogfood log: /deep:review --depth-mode=expansive, fan-out opus + deepseek\n2: \n3: > Kept from the conductor's session scratchpad. Paths under `D/` named the conductor's scratch evidence, which was not kept; the packet paths (`R/`, `SPEC/`) still resolve.\n4: \n5: Run on the integration worktree at `de32abbb74d`. Spec folder\n6: `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode`.\n7: Scratch evidence lives beside this file in `scratchpad/dogfood/`.\n8: `D` below means that scratch directory, and `R` means the packet's `review/` directory.\n9: \n10: ## Setup and invocation\n11: \n12: ### F1. The dry run cannot preview a fan-out run's lineage commands\n13: \n14: - What happened: with `--restart`, the first `dry_run_boundary` is `step_apply_lifecycle_request`\n15:   (state-mutation). Without `--restart` it is the fan-out `step_frontier_seed`. So `dry_run_halt`\n16:   always lands before `step_fanout_spawn`.\n17: - `fanout-run.cjs` has no dry-run flag of its own (its `FANOUT_FLAGS` list is at line 30).\n18: - The operator cannot confirm the model, effort, config dir or focus from the documented dry run.\n19: - I previewed read-only through the exported builders instead (`D/preview.mjs`, `D/preview2.log`).\n20: - Evidence: `D/dry-run-halt.jsonl`, `deep-review.yaml:256` and `deep-review.yaml:338`.\n21: - Severity for the operator: a UX gap. The documented pre-flight tells you nothing about the\n22:   lineages it exists to protect.\n23: \n24: ### F2. A default cli-claude-code fan-out lineage cannot run Bash, so it cannot record state\n25: \n26: - `buildClaudeLineageCommand` passes `--permission-mode acceptEdits` when no `sandboxMode` is set.\n27:   `resolveClaudePermissionMode` resolves the default `workspace-write` to `acceptEdits`\n28:   (`executor-config.ts`, near line 624).\n29: - Probe: `claude -p ... --permission-mode acceptEdits` on `~/.claude-account2`, asked to run\n30:   `node -e 'console.log(40+2)'`.\n31:   - Reply: \"I couldn't run it: the command needs your approval\".\n32:   - Exit status: **0** (`D/probe/claude-probe.out`).\n33: - The lineage contract requires Bash for the append gateway and the reducer\n34:   (`fanout-run.cjs` `buildLoopPrompt`, around line 1725).\n35: - So a cli-claude-code lineage built from the documented `--executor=cli-claude-code ...` flag\n36:   group cannot write a single state row on a config dir without a `node` allow rule. Its process\n37:   still exits 0.\n38: - The `--executor` flag group has no sandbox flag (`review.md` flag table; presentation asset lines\n39:   139-147). The only way to set `sandboxMode` is an `--executors` JSON matrix.\n40: - Judgment call: I set `sandboxMode: \"danger-full-access\"` on the opus lineage, which gives\n41:   `--permission-mode bypassPermissions`. The probe with that mode printed `42`\n42:   (`D/probe/claude-probe2.out`).\n43: - That puts opus on the same footing as the deepseek lineage, which the builder already runs with\n44:   `--auto`. Write containment still runs in preserve mode.\n45: - A PreToolUse hook on this host raised the same risk as an advisory\n46:   (`non-interactive-permission-mode-risk`).\n47: \n48: ### F3. cli-opencode v2 carries the effort as `-m model#max`, not `--variant`\n49: \n50: - opencode on this host is `v2.3.2`, so the builder takes the non-v1 branch\n51:   (`fanout-run.cjs:2669-2690`): `run --standalone -m opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max --format json --auto`.\n52: - `--variant` is the v1 branch only (`fanout-run.cjs:2651`).\n53: - The presentation asset's executor list still documents only `--variant`\n54:   (`deep-review-presentation.txt:220`).\n55: - `pinReasoningEffortForModel` forces `max` on any flash-pinned model anyway\n56:   (`fanout-run.cjs:2614`), so `--reasoning-effort=max` changes nothing here.\n57: \n58: ### F4. Stale defaults and examples\n59: \n60: - `CLAUDE_DEFAULT_MODEL = 'claude-opus-4-8'` (`fanout-run.cjs:2755`). The current id,\n61:   `claude-opus-5-5`, is accepted (`D/probe/claude-probe2.out`), but an operator who leaves off\n62:   `--model` gets an older model.\n63: - The presentation example uses `--label=` with an empty value for the opencode lineage\n64:   (`deep-review-presentation.txt:495`). The label schema requires `/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/`, so the\n65:   example as written would fail parsing.\n66: \n67: ### F5. The restart lineage is lost on the fan-out path\n68: \n69: - `step_apply_lifecycle_request` binds `prior_session_id` and `prior_generation`. Here that was\n70:   generation 2 (`D/prior-lineage.json`), and the step archived `review/` to\n71:   `review-archive/20261119T183614Z`.\n72: - The fan-out parent never runs `step_create_config`, so nothing records generation 3 or the parent\n73:   session. Each lineage then writes `lineage_mode: auto` as a fresh run (`buildLoopPrompt` setup\n74:   bindings).\n75: - The archive happens, but the lineage chain the restart contract promises\n76:   (`generation+1, parentSessionId`) does not.\n77: \n78: ### F6. The seed step's budget line describes a run that will not exist\n79: \n80: - The parent seed printed `budget after seed 24 iterations, 6 growth slots` (`D/seed.err`).\n81: - In fan-out, each lineage is sized separately: 24 iterations from its share of 3 nodes, so a node\n82:   cap of 12 and 9 growth slots per lineage (`fanout-run.cjs` `expansiveLineageBudgets`;\n83:   `D/fanout.err`).\n84: - The parent figure is neither the per-lineage nor the total budget, and nothing says so.\n85: - `fanout-run.cjs` does print the correct per-lineage lines, and they are good:\n86:   `lineage opus budget 24 iterations, derived from its seed share`.\n87: \n88: ## Target and seeds\n89: \n90: ### Target choice\n91: \n92: - Target: `21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep .skilled/agents .claude/agents .codex/agents .pi/agents .dsh/agents .vibe/agents (...)`,\n93:   type `files`.\n94: - Why:\n95:   - Of 513,900 added lines, 488,790 sit under `specs/`.\n96:   - The prior review used the same label-around-range shape.\n97:   - The range-plus-pathspec form keeps git's own syntax, and `isCommitRange` reads any range token\n98:     in the text as a range (`frontier-admit.cjs:591-603`).\n99: - Admission does not enforce the path narrowing. For a commit range, relevance reads each lineage's\n100:   `reviewScopeFiles` (`frontier-admit.cjs:632-638`), which the leaf fills during scope discovery.\n101: - The `files` branch of `step_scope_discovery` says \"expand glob patterns ... validate all files\n102:   exist\" and has no commit-range branch (`deep-review.yaml:815-820`). The range form therefore\n103:   depends on the leaf reading the label correctly. That is a contract gap.\n104: \n105: ### Seeds: 6 admitted, 1 pruned\n106: \n107: - I chose 6 seeds rather than the allowed 8.\n108:   - Each lineage dealt a node derives 24 iterations, and the depth-1 band is `0.5 x 24 = 12`.\n109:   - Three nodes at 4 dimensions is exactly 12. Eight seeds would have under-funded one node per\n110:     lineage.\n111:   - `review.md` says this itself: set `--max-iterations` to at least\n112:     `2 * ceil(nodes/lineages) * dimensions`.\n113: - Admitted: F-1-002 (frontier-admit.cjs), F-1-003 (fanout run/merge), F-1-004 (command surface),\n114:   F-1-005 (reducers/upsert/convergence), F-1-006 (docs, agents and mirrors), F-1-007 (divergent\n115:   pivot, continuity, coverage graph).\n116: - Pruned: F-1-001 `generated-artifact` (compiled routing manifest, skill graph, graph metadata,\n117:   compiled contracts). Evidence: `D/seed.out` and `R/frontier-nodes.jsonl`.\n118: - No merge commit qualified for `merge-no-own-diff`. All 17 merges in the range bring in feature\n119:   work against their first parent, so the prune vocabulary had nothing to say about them.\n120: - Prune ids are allocated before the admitted ids (`frontier-admit.cjs:835-859`), so a pruned row\n121:   takes `F-1-001` whatever its position in the input. That is harmless, but it surprises when you\n122:   read the partition.\n123: - Deal (round-robin by node id): opus = F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006; deepseek = F-1-003, F-1-005,\n124:   F-1-007 (`R/orchestration-status.log`).\n125: \n126: ## Run progress\n127: \n128: (appended below as the run proceeds)\n129: \n130: ### P1. Scope discovery differs by lineage on the same range target (status at +6 min)\n131: \n132: - **opus** recorded `reviewScopeFiles` as 232 touched files and no `specs/` paths.\n133: - **deepseek** recorded the 8 pathspec directories verbatim as its scope files\n134:   (`R/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-config.json`). It took the label's paths as the file list and\n135:   did not expand the range.\n136: - Both are \"valid\" under `scopeInsideTouchedFiles`, because a directory entry contains every file\n137:   under it. The relevance check is therefore much looser on deepseek, which could admit a sub-target\n138:   for a file the range never touched.\n139: - Root cause: `step_scope_discovery` has no commit-range branch (`deep-review.yaml:815-820`), so\n140:   each model improvises.\n141: - Opus raised this gap on its own as a depth-2 frontier proposal at its first iteration:\n142:   `F-2-007`, under F-1-002, asking \"Does any workflow step give a commit-range review target its\n143:   touched files\" (`R/lineages/opus/frontier-nodes.jsonl`).\n144: - Timing: opus landed 2 iterations in about 5 minutes. Each state row carries\n145:   `durationMs: 300000`, which looks like a placeholder value rather than a measured one. Deepseek\n146:   had written its config and dashboard but no iteration yet.\n147: - Liveness: the stall watchdog did not fire on opus, even though `--output-format text` streams\n148:   nothing. The artifact poller counts lineage writes as progress (`fanout-run.cjs:2219-2234`), and\n149:   the ledger shows a `progress` heartbeat every 60 s for both lineages.\n150: \n151: ### P2. The deepseek lineage died at +10 min on provider quota, after one iteration\n152: \n153: - `R/orchestration-status.log` line 23: `failed`, `failure_class: quota`, `retry_verdict: fatal`,\n154:   `terminal: true`, `duration_ms: 596027`.\n155: - The provider body said: \"OpenCode Go monthly usage limit reached ... resets in 13d 13h\"\n156:   (HTTP 429, `retryAfterMs: 1171152000`). See the tail of `R/lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out`.\n157: - Good: the runner classified the error correctly and did not burn retries on a 429 with a 13-day\n158:   reset.\n159: - Bad, as UX:\n160:   - Nothing pre-flights the provider quota. `preflightFanoutCapabilities` checks binaries only.\n161:   - The failure appears only in the ledger. The running fan-out process prints nothing to stderr\n162:     about a dead lineage, so an operator watching the terminal sees no signal for the rest of the\n163:     run.\n164:   - A 2-lineage review silently becomes a 1-lineage review. The merge will report whatever it\n165:     reports.\n166: - Cost data: opencode-go JSON carried `\"cost\":0` on every `step_finish` (the subscription plan), and\n167:   token counts are present. The claude lineage, with `--output-format text`, carries no token or\n168:   cost data at all.\n169: - Recovery decision (my judgment call, recorded):\n170:   - The same model is served by LLM Gateway as `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`. That id is\n171:     the runner's own `OPENCODE_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`fanout-run.cjs:2756`), and the presentation asset\n172:     names both ids as the same DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (`deep-review-presentation.txt:226`).\n173:   - The probe returned `42` and reported cost `0.000069834` (`D/probe/oc-probe.out`).\n174:   - Once opus settles, I re-dispatch only the `deepseek` label through `fanout-run.cjs` with\n175:     `--allow-single-lineage`, the same lineage directory and the new model. The lineage resumes its\n176:     stored session and frontier store.\n177:   - It is not done concurrently: two runners would share one `orchestration-status.log`, and\n178:     `markOrphanedLineages` reads that ledger at start.\n179: - Contract gap: there is no documented way to re-run one failed lineage of a fan-out. The only\n180:   route is the internal `--allow-single-lineage` flag, which the runner's own refusal text describes\n181:   as leaving the workflow.\n182: \n183: ### P3. The opus lineage stopped converged at run 15 of 24, in 28.5 min (18:36:58 to 19:05:31)\n184: \n185: - Timing:\n186:   - 14 iterations, about 1.4 to 4 min each. The `D/fanout.out` summary records `duration_ms: 1712943`.\n187:   - That is far below the 7 to 8 minutes per iteration that `review.md:100` warns about.\n188:   - `maxDurationMinutes` (120) never came into play.\n189: - Stop path:\n190:   - Stuck recovery fired twice: `stuckRecovery` events at runs 10 and 13.\n191:   - A `blocked_stop` at run 14 came from `graphlessFallbackGate`, reason\n192:     `add-cited-fallback-ledger-rows`.\n193:   - Then `terminal_gates` returned `stopReason: converged` at run 15.\n194:   - Then `synthesis_incomplete`, reason `synthesis_artifact_invariant_failed`, invariant\n195:     `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`.\n196:   - All of these are in `R/lineages/opus/deep-review-state.jsonl`.\n197: - Registry loss:\n198:   - The deltas hold 18 findings (3 P1, 15 P2). The registry holds 14 open (2 P1, 12 P2).\n199:   - `OPUS-REC-P1-003` and `OPUS-F006-P2-003` are missing.\n200:   - `OPUS-F004-P1-001` folded into `OPUS-F002-P2-002`, which the registry now shows as P1.\n201:   - The lineage flagged the loss itself, but the runner still marked the lineage `fulfilled`\n202:     (`D/fanout.out`).\n203: - Frontier behavior (`R/lineages/opus/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the registry `frontier` block):\n204:   - F-1-002 and F-1-006 were answered with all four dimensions.\n205:   - F-1-004 (the command surface) was closed `exhausted/stuck` at run 10. Its node-bound passes\n206:     were correctness, security and traceability only. Its maintainability pass was never\n207:     dispatched.\n208:   - The stuck counter that closed it was built from two clean passes on *other* nodes: run 8 on\n209:     F-1-002, ratio 0, and run 9 on F-1-006, ratio 0.036. Both sit at or below the no-progress\n210:     cutoff, which is `0.5 x 0.10 = 0.05` (`convergence.cjs:757`, `:1387`).\n211:   - F-2-007 was admitted at run 1: one growth proposal, depth 2, under F-1-002. It got one pass\n212:     (correctness, run 12) and was closed `exhausted/stuck` at run 13. Run 12 found a new issue\n213:     but reported ratio 0.05, which counts as no-progress.\n214:   - So the expansive mode's \"do not stop while nodes are open\" promise is defeated by a stuck\n215:     counter that is lineage-wide rather than per node. The run converged with one depth-1 node a\n216:     dimension short and the depth-2 node three dimensions short, and `searchDebt` reads 0.\n217:   - The reviewer found this independently (OPUS-F004-P1-002, OPUS-REC-P1-003), from inside the run\n218:     it was reviewing.\n219: - The registry reports F-1-004's covered dimensions as all four, although no node-bound\n220:   maintainability pass ran. Run 13's recovery pass, not bound to a node, appears to be credited to\n221:   it. That is misleading on the dashboard.\n222: - Growth: 1 proposal admitted (F-2-007) against 9 available growth slots, and none pruned. Opus\n223:   proposed sparingly.\n224: - Writes outside `review/`: the runner's `metadata_refresh` rewrote the packet's\n225:   `description.json` at settle (`R/orchestration-status.log`, `metadata_refresh_ok`\n226:   `generate-description.js`). That is expected per `metadataRefreshRequested`, but it is a write\n227:   outside the artifact dir that the operator did not ask for.\n228: \n229: ### P4. Provider exhaustion: how the runner handled it\n230: \n231: All times are UTC. The ledger writes UTC, and file mtimes show local time (UTC+1), which misleads\n232: when the two are read side by side.\n233: \n234: - **Timeline**\n235:   - 18:37:03: deepseek spawned on `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max`, as pid 60602.\n236:   - 18:37:21: the first opencode JSON event.\n237:   - The lineage worked for about 9.5 minutes. It wrote its config, strategy, dashboard and\n238:     `iteration-001.md`: 1 iteration, 292 JSON events.\n239:   - 18:46:52.767: opencode emitted a single `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event, `provider.go-limit`, HTTP 429:\n240:     \"OpenCode Go monthly usage limit reached ... resets in 13d 13h\". The quota ran out\n241:     *mid-run*, not at launch.\n242:   - 18:46:54.538: the runner recorded `failed` with `failure_class: quota`,\n243:     `retry_verdict: fatal`, `retryable: false` and `terminal: true`, about **1.8 s** after the error\n244:     event.\n245: - **Did it fail loud or hang? It failed loud in the ledger, fast and correctly.**\n246:   - opencode exited with code 1 straight away. There was no hang and no stall-watchdog involvement.\n247:   - The runner's failure classifier read the provider body, and with no retries the remaining\n248:     13-day reset was not wasted.\n249:   - The opus lineage kept running unaffected, as `gauges.failed` went to 1.\n250: - **Did the operator see it? Not unless they read the ledger.**\n251:   - `fanout-run.cjs` wrote nothing to stderr about the failure. `D/fanout.err` holds only the two\n252:     budget lines and the `--auto` warning.\n253:   - It kept printing `progress` heartbeats for opus only.\n254:   - The conductor (me) noticed at the next poll, 18:59, about **12 minutes after the failure**.\n255:   - The final JSON on stdout and the process exit code 2 (`status: partial`) did carry it, but only\n256:     once the whole fan-out ended, 18 minutes later.\n257: - **Pre-flight**: `preflightFanoutCapabilities` checks binaries, not provider quota. A launch-time\n258:   probe would not have caught this case anyway, because the quota ran out after the launch.\n259: - **Recovery cost**:\n260:   - There is no documented single-lineage rerun.\n261:   - I used `fanout-run.cjs --allow-single-lineage` with a one-entry matrix\n262:     (`R/fanout-config-recovery.json`) under the same `--base-artifact-dir` and the same label\n263:     `deepseek`. It reuses `lineages/deepseek/`, so the stored session id and frontier store\n264:     carry over.\n265:   - It was launched 19:06:04, after opus settled, as runner pid 57919, lineage pid 59596, watchdog\n266:     pid 57920 at 180 min.\n267:   - The built command, confirmed from the live process and `lineages/deepseek/invocation-metadata.json`:\n268:     `opencode run --standalone -m llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max --format json --auto`,\n269:     model `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, `reasoningEffort: max`.\n270:   - Route (a) was accepted: `cli-opencode` takes the `llmgateway/` prefix. Vibe was not needed.\n271: - **Deviation**: the coordinator later asked for a dry run before the rerun. The rerun was already\n272:   live by then, launched on my own judgment at 19:06. The checks it did get were the provider probe\n273:   (`D/probe/oc-probe.out`, prints `42`) and the live process arguments, not a pre-launch preview.\n274:   The workflow's dry run cannot show fan-out lineage commands anyway (F1).\n275: - **The lineage clock**: the resumed lineage keeps its `createdAt` of 18:41:16 and its\n276:   `maxDurationMinutes` of 120. Its duration stop therefore falls around 20:41 UTC, so the recovery\n277:   has about 95 minutes, not 120. The 9.5 minutes lost to the quota failure and the 19 minutes spent\n278:   waiting for opus both count against it.\n279: \n280: ### P5. The deepseek recovery is running (status 19:17 UTC)\n281: \n282: - The resume worked as hoped:\n283:   - Iteration 1 from the dead attempt was kept: F-1-003 correctness, timestamp 18:45:15.\n284:   - The recovery continued at iteration 2 (F-1-005 correctness, 19:12:21) and iteration 3\n285:     (F-1-007 correctness, 19:16:25), in the same `lineages/deepseek/` dir and node store.\n286: - Pace is about 4 to 5 min per iteration, against opus's 1.4 to 4 min. Opus finished its whole\n287:   14-iteration lineage in less time than deepseek needs for about 6 iterations.\n288: - Lineage differences in artifact shape:\n289:   - Opus appended an `active` row to `frontier-nodes.jsonl` on every node visit; 17 rows for 4\n290:     nodes.\n291:   - Deepseek appends none. Its store still holds only the 3 `open` seed rows, so node activity is\n292:     visible only through the reducer's registry projection, not the store.\n293:   - Deepseek's state rows carry `timestamp` values rounded to whole seconds (`...:21.000Z`).\n294:     Opus's carry milliseconds.\n295:   - Opus's `durationMs` was a flat 300000 on every row.\n296: \n297: ### P6. The deepseek recovery finished, but 9 of its 12 iterations look rubber-stamped\n298: \n299: - The runner finished 19:25:56 with `status: ok`, the lineage `fulfilled` and exit 0, after 19.9 min\n300:   (`D/rec.out`).\n301: - On paper, the lineage did 12 iterations and answered all 3 nodes (F-1-003, F-1-005 and F-1-007)\n302:   with all four dimensions each.\n303: - The shape says otherwise:\n304:   - Iterations 4 to 12 were written 20 to 60 s apart (iteration file mtimes 19:18:05 to 19:23:38\n305:     UTC).\n306:   - Each record claims a whole-minute timestamp (19:18:00, 19:19:00 ... 19:26:00).\n307:   - Iteration 12's record says 19:26:00, *after* the lineage's own `synthesis_incomplete` row at\n308:     19:25:13 and after the runner recorded the lineage complete at 19:25:56.\n309:   - Six of the nine passes report 0 findings. The narratives shrink from about 1,300 words\n310:     (iterations 1 to 3) to 570 to 820 words.\n311: - The lineage never ran the stop gates. Its state log has no `terminal_gates`, `stuckRecovery` or\n312:   `blocked_stop` row, even though passes 6 to 11 all had ratio 0, which would have tripped stuck\n313:   recovery twice under opus's rules. It ends straight on `synthesis_incomplete` with\n314:   `stopReason: converged`.\n315: - The runner's timestamp-window check (`fanout-run.cjs`, `timestamp_anomaly` in `D/rec.out`)\n316:   flagged only the 2 legitimate pre-resume rows (`before_window`). It missed the future-stamped row,\n317:   which sits inside its 120 s tolerance.\n318: - **The biggest behavioral gap between the two lineages:**\n319:   - Opus executed the workflow's per-iteration convergence and stop steps: stuck recovery, the\n320:     blocked stop and the legal terminal gates.\n321:   - Deepseek, given the same prompt, skipped them and stamped out the remaining dimension passes.\n322:   - The fan-out runner accepted both as `fulfilled`. Nothing in the completion contract checks that\n323:     a CLI lineage ran the stop gates before it claims `converged`.\n324: \n325: ### P7. Merge, verdict and closeout on the fan-out root\n326: \n327: - `fanout-merge.cjs` returned `merged_verdict: CONDITIONAL`, P0 0, P1 4, P2 18, `search_debt: 0`,\n328:   and `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`).\n329: - The counts are an exact sum of the two lineage registries (opus 2/12, deepseek 2/6). No\n330:   cross-lineage dedupe happened. That is correct here, because no two findings named the same\n331:   file:line.\n332: - `review-verdict.cjs` gave CONDITIONAL (`D/verdict.out`).\n333: - `synthesis-closeout.cjs` on the root wrote a `synthesis_incomplete` row with\n334:   `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`, 26 against 22, and `runId: \"review\"`.\n335:   - The runId is the artifact folder name, because a fan-out root has no config\n336:     (`synthesis-closeout.cjs:280-289`).\n337:   - Both lineages wrote the same invariant failure.\n338: - **Correction to P3: the registry lost nothing.** All 4 \"missing\" ids, 3 from opus and 1 from\n339:   deepseek, were recorded as *refinements* of an earlier finding. The registry keeps the earlier id,\n340:   takes the refined title and severity, and logs the transition\n341:   `\"Refinement of an earlier finding\"`. Examples:\n342:   - `OPUS-REC-P1-003` into `OPUS-F004-P1-002`.\n343:   - `OPUS-F004-P1-001` into `OPUS-F002-P2-002`, raised to P1.\n344:   - `R2-P2-001` into `R1-P2-002`.\n345: - So the invariant check is a **false alarm**: it compares delta ids against registry ids and does\n346:   not understand refinements. The real friction is twofold:\n347:   - Every run that refines a finding reports \"synthesis incomplete\".\n348:   - A refined finding keeps an id that names the wrong iteration and severity:\n349:     `OPUS-F002-P2-002` is a P1 whose title came from iteration 7.\n350: - `step_update_config_status` cannot run on a fan-out root, because there is no root config to mark\n351:   complete. `step_emit_resource_map` and `step_refresh_completed_dashboard` both skip on fan-out, so\n352:   the root has **no dashboard at all**. The operator gets two lineage dashboards, the attribution\n353:   file and the report.\n354: \n355: ### P8. Save phase\n356: \n357: - `generate-context.js` without `--full-auto` is documented as plan-only (`deep-review.yaml:2556`\n358:   requirements).\n359: - It still rewrote the packet's `description.json`: it bumped `memorySequence` to 4, appended a\n360:   `memoryNameHistory` entry and set `lastUpdated` to 19:28:51.\n361: - The fan-out runner's settle-time `metadata_refresh` had already replaced that file's\n362:   `description` and `keywords` with text auto-extracted from `spec.md` (\"The deep-research and\n363:   deep-review loops converge on the three to five questions ...\").\n364: - Both writes were outside `review/`, and neither was asked for. I restored the file to HEAD\n365:   (`git restore`), because the tree was clean at the start and the operator wants no doc edits.\n366: - **Deviation from the workflow:** I skipped `step_generate_context --full-auto`, the continuity\n367:   write into packet docs, for the same reason.\n368: \n369: ### P9. Lineage differences, side by side\n370: \n371: | Aspect | opus (cli-claude-code, claude-opus-5-5, medium) | deepseek (cli-opencode) |\n372: |---|---|---|\n373: | Launch | needed `sandboxMode: danger-full-access`. Default `acceptEdits` cannot run Bash in `-p` mode (F2) | default resolves to `--auto` with a FATAL WARN banner |\n374: | Provider | ran clean | opencode-go hit its monthly quota after 9.5 min; relaunched on llmgateway |\n375: | Wall clock | 28.5 min for 14 iterations | 9.9 min (1 iteration) + 19.9 min (11 iterations) |\n376: | Per-iteration time | 1.4 to 4 min, evenly spread | 4 to 9 min for real passes, then 20 to 60 s rubber stamps |\n377: | Scope discovery | 232 touched files | 8 pathspec directories |\n378: | Node store rows | appends `active` per visit (17 rows) | none past the seed (3 rows) |\n379: | Stop machinery | stuck x2, blocked stop, terminal gates | none recorded |\n380: | Growth proposals | 1 (F-2-007) | 0 |\n381: | Findings | 18 deltas, 14 registry (2 P1) | 9 deltas, 8 registry (2 P1) |\n382: | Timestamps | millisecond precision; `durationMs` a flat 300000 | whole seconds or whole minutes, one in the future |\n383: | Cost data | none (text output) | token counts per step; cost 0 on opencode-go, real cost on llmgateway |\n384: \n385: ### P10. Report and dashboard clarity\n386: \n387: - With no root dashboard and no root config, the per-run \"what happened\" view of a fan-out review\n388:   is scattered across:\n389:   - `orchestration-status.log` (UTC, one heartbeat per lineage per minute)\n390:   - two lineage dashboards\n391:   - `fanout-attribution.md`\n392:   - the merged registry\n393: - `fanout-attribution.md` is the closest thing to a summary.\n394: - The runner's stdout JSON is the only place the final per-lineage status appears, and it is\n395:   machine-shaped.\n396: - The duration estimate in `review.md:100` (\"seven to eight minutes an iteration\") was wrong in\n397:   both directions: opus averaged about 2 minutes, and deepseek's real passes took 4 to 9.\n398: \n399: ## Stop reasons and totals\n400: \n401: - **opus**: `converged` (terminal gates at run 15), 14 iterations, 28.5 min.\n402: - **deepseek**:\n403:   - First attempt: `quota` failure, 1 iteration, 9.9 min.\n404:   - Recovery: `converged`, recorded only in `synthesis_incomplete` with no terminal gates, 11 more\n405:     iterations, 19.9 min.\n406: - **Fan-out wall clock**: 18:36:58 to 19:25:56, 49 min including the 30 s handover between runs.\n407:   Root synthesis followed until 19:28.\n408: - `maxDurationMinutes` (120) and the 180-min watchdogs never fired.\n409: \n410: ## Commit\n411: \n412: Commit `a424fb6cd8a` on `worktrees/455-expansive-depth-integration` stages the whole artifact dir, as `step_stage_artifact_dir` does:\n413: `review/` (root, both lineages and the raw lineage logs) plus `review-archive/20261119T183614Z/`.\n414: The tree was clean after the commit. All captured PIDs (57348, 57349, 57919, 57920) had exited by then; none was killed.\n415: \n416: ## Late checks\n417: \n418: - **F2 re-checked from the integration root**, where Claude Code also loads the repo's\n419:   `.claude/settings.json`. That file has `allow: []`. The same refusal came back with exit 0\n420:   (`D/probe/claude-probe3.out`). F2 stands as a contract bug rather than a probe artifact.\n421: - **R2-P1-001 is reachable**: `thought` is an allowed review status (`.skilled/agents/deep-review.md:236`).\n422: - **R3-P1-001**: no decision in `011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md` supersedes REQ-007's\n423:   pivot admission. It is a live spec/YAML contradiction, so the fix is a Logic-Sync choice: amend\n424:   the spec or implement the admission.\n425: - **The resumed lineage overwrote the failed attempt's raw log**:\n426:   - The committed `lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out` holds one session, the llmgateway\n427:     recovery. The opencode-go attempt and its 429 body survive only in the ledger's `failed` row.\n428:   - Sums for the committed log: 188 steps, 603,093 input, 80,386 output, 96,064 reasoning,\n429:     51,752,832 cache-read tokens, cost $0.4202.\n430:   - The opus lineage log holds only its 3.7 KB final text answer, so it carries no token data.\n431: - **Secrets scan** of both committed lineage logs found no email address or key. The 429 body that\n432:   carries the OpenCode workspace id and console URL lives in the ledger\n433:   (`review/orchestration-status.log`), which is committed. That is flagged only.\n434: - **Correction to the coordinator's framing** (\"the registry lost 2 and folded 1\"): every one of the\n435:   4 missing ids is a refinement kept under an earlier id. One side effect is real: a refinement\n436:   keeps the earlier file:line. `OPUS-F004-P1-001`'s location, `deep-review.yaml:815`, now survives\n437:   only as `frontier-admit.cjs:618`. The real \"fulfilled\" problem is P6: deepseek was accepted with\n438:   no stop-gate rows at all.\n439: - **Coverage caveat**: deepseek's security, traceability and maintainability passes on fan-out,\n440:   reducers and pivot (F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007) were the 20 to 60 s stamps. Zero P0 on those\n441:   surfaces means *not examined*, not clean.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-review-gen2.md, lines 1-441\n1: # Dogfood log: /deep:review --depth-mode=expansive, fan-out opus + deepseek\n2: \n3: > Kept from the conductor's session scratchpad. Paths under `D/` named the conductor's scratch evidence, which was not kept; the packet paths (`R/`, `SPEC/`) still resolve.\n4: \n5: Run on the integration worktree at `de32abbb74d`. Spec folder\n6: `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode`.\n7: Scratch evidence lives beside this file in `scratchpad/dogfood/`.\n8: `D` below means that scratch directory, and `R` means the packet's `review/` directory.\n9: \n10: ## Setup and invocation\n11: \n12: ### F1. The dry run cannot preview a fan-out run's lineage commands\n13: \n14: - What happened: with `--restart`, the first `dry_run_boundary` is `step_apply_lifecycle_request`\n15:   (state-mutation). Without `--restart` it is the fan-out `step_frontier_seed`. So `dry_run_halt`\n16:   always lands before `step_fanout_spawn`.\n17: - `fanout-run.cjs` has no dry-run flag of its own (its `FANOUT_FLAGS` list is at line 30).\n18: - The operator cannot confirm the model, effort, config dir or focus from the documented dry run.\n19: - I previewed read-only through the exported builders instead (`D/preview.mjs`, `D/preview2.log`).\n20: - Evidence: `D/dry-run-halt.jsonl`, `deep-review.yaml:256` and `deep-review.yaml:338`.\n21: - Severity for the operator: a UX gap. The documented pre-flight tells you nothing about the\n22:   lineages it exists to protect.\n23: \n24: ### F2. A default cli-claude-code fan-out lineage cannot run Bash, so it cannot record state\n25: \n26: - `buildClaudeLineageCommand` passes `--permission-mode acceptEdits` when no `sandboxMode` is set.\n27:   `resolveClaudePermissionMode` resolves the default `workspace-write` to `acceptEdits`\n28:   (`executor-config.ts`, near line 624).\n29: - Probe: `claude -p ... --permission-mode acceptEdits` on `~/.claude-account2`, asked to run\n30:   `node -e 'console.log(40+2)'`.\n31:   - Reply: \"I couldn't run it: the command needs your approval\".\n32:   - Exit status: **0** (`D/probe/claude-probe.out`).\n33: - The lineage contract requires Bash for the append gateway and the reducer\n34:   (`fanout-run.cjs` `buildLoopPrompt`, around line 1725).\n35: - So a cli-claude-code lineage built from the documented `--executor=cli-claude-code ...` flag\n36:   group cannot write a single state row on a config dir without a `node` allow rule. Its process\n37:   still exits 0.\n38: - The `--executor` flag group has no sandbox flag (`review.md` flag table; presentation asset lines\n39:   139-147). The only way to set `sandboxMode` is an `--executors` JSON matrix.\n40: - Judgment call: I set `sandboxMode: \"danger-full-access\"` on the opus lineage, which gives\n41:   `--permission-mode bypassPermissions`. The probe with that mode printed `42`\n42:   (`D/probe/claude-probe2.out`).\n43: - That puts opus on the same footing as the deepseek lineage, which the builder already runs with\n44:   `--auto`. Write containment still runs in preserve mode.\n45: - A PreToolUse hook on this host raised the same risk as an advisory\n46:   (`non-interactive-permission-mode-risk`).\n47: \n48: ### F3. cli-opencode v2 carries the effort as `-m model#max`, not `--variant`\n49: \n50: - opencode on this host is `v2.3.2`, so the builder takes the non-v1 branch\n51:   (`fanout-run.cjs:2669-2690`): `run --standalone -m opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max --format json --auto`.\n52: - `--variant` is the v1 branch only (`fanout-run.cjs:2651`).\n53: - The presentation asset's executor list still documents only `--variant`\n54:   (`deep-review-presentation.txt:220`).\n55: - `pinReasoningEffortForModel` forces `max` on any flash-pinned model anyway\n56:   (`fanout-run.cjs:2614`), so `--reasoning-effort=max` changes nothing here.\n57: \n58: ### F4. Stale defaults and examples\n59: \n60: - `CLAUDE_DEFAULT_MODEL = 'claude-opus-4-8'` (`fanout-run.cjs:2755`). The current id,\n61:   `claude-opus-5-5`, is accepted (`D/probe/claude-probe2.out`), but an operator who leaves off\n62:   `--model` gets an older model.\n63: - The presentation example uses `--label=` with an empty value for the opencode lineage\n64:   (`deep-review-presentation.txt:495`). The label schema requires `/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$/`, so the\n65:   example as written would fail parsing.\n66: \n67: ### F5. The restart lineage is lost on the fan-out path\n68: \n69: - `step_apply_lifecycle_request` binds `prior_session_id` and `prior_generation`. Here that was\n70:   generation 2 (`D/prior-lineage.json`), and the step archived `review/` to\n71:   `review-archive/20261119T183614Z`.\n72: - The fan-out parent never runs `step_create_config`, so nothing records generation 3 or the parent\n73:   session. Each lineage then writes `lineage_mode: auto` as a fresh run (`buildLoopPrompt` setup\n74:   bindings).\n75: - The archive happens, but the lineage chain the restart contract promises\n76:   (`generation+1, parentSessionId`) does not.\n77: \n78: ### F6. The seed step's budget line describes a run that will not exist\n79: \n80: - The parent seed printed `budget after seed 24 iterations, 6 growth slots` (`D/seed.err`).\n81: - In fan-out, each lineage is sized separately: 24 iterations from its share of 3 nodes, so a node\n82:   cap of 12 and 9 growth slots per lineage (`fanout-run.cjs` `expansiveLineageBudgets`;\n83:   `D/fanout.err`).\n84: - The parent figure is neither the per-lineage nor the total budget, and nothing says so.\n85: - `fanout-run.cjs` does print the correct per-lineage lines, and they are good:\n86:   `lineage opus budget 24 iterations, derived from its seed share`.\n87: \n88: ## Target and seeds\n89: \n90: ### Target choice\n91: \n92: - Target: `21c4b325b5a..de32abbb74d -- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop .skilled/commands/deep .skilled/agents .claude/agents .codex/agents .pi/agents .dsh/agents .vibe/agents (...)`,\n93:   type `files`.\n94: - Why:\n95:   - Of 513,900 added lines, 488,790 sit under `specs/`.\n96:   - The prior review used the same label-around-range shape.\n97:   - The range-plus-pathspec form keeps git's own syntax, and `isCommitRange` reads any range token\n98:     in the text as a range (`frontier-admit.cjs:591-603`).\n99: - Admission does not enforce the path narrowing. For a commit range, relevance reads each lineage's\n100:   `reviewScopeFiles` (`frontier-admit.cjs:632-638`), which the leaf fills during scope discovery.\n101: - The `files` branch of `step_scope_discovery` says \"expand glob patterns ... validate all files\n102:   exist\" and has no commit-range branch (`deep-review.yaml:815-820`). The range form therefore\n103:   depends on the leaf reading the label correctly. That is a contract gap.\n104: \n105: ### Seeds: 6 admitted, 1 pruned\n106: \n107: - I chose 6 seeds rather than the allowed 8.\n108:   - Each lineage dealt a node derives 24 iterations, and the depth-1 band is `0.5 x 24 = 12`.\n109:   - Three nodes at 4 dimensions is exactly 12. Eight seeds would have under-funded one node per\n110:     lineage.\n111:   - `review.md` says this itself: set `--max-iterations` to at least\n112:     `2 * ceil(nodes/lineages) * dimensions`.\n113: - Admitted: F-1-002 (frontier-admit.cjs), F-1-003 (fanout run/merge), F-1-004 (command surface),\n114:   F-1-005 (reducers/upsert/convergence), F-1-006 (docs, agents and mirrors), F-1-007 (divergent\n115:   pivot, continuity, coverage graph).\n116: - Pruned: F-1-001 `generated-artifact` (compiled routing manifest, skill graph, graph metadata,\n117:   compiled contracts). Evidence: `D/seed.out` and `R/frontier-nodes.jsonl`.\n118: - No merge commit qualified for `merge-no-own-diff`. All 17 merges in the range bring in feature\n119:   work against their first parent, so the prune vocabulary had nothing to say about them.\n120: - Prune ids are allocated before the admitted ids (`frontier-admit.cjs:835-859`), so a pruned row\n121:   takes `F-1-001` whatever its position in the input. That is harmless, but it surprises when you\n122:   read the partition.\n123: - Deal (round-robin by node id): opus = F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006; deepseek = F-1-003, F-1-005,\n124:   F-1-007 (`R/orchestration-status.log`).\n125: \n126: ## Run progress\n127: \n128: (appended below as the run proceeds)\n129: \n130: ### P1. Scope discovery differs by lineage on the same range target (status at +6 min)\n131: \n132: - **opus** recorded `reviewScopeFiles` as 232 touched files and no `specs/` paths.\n133: - **deepseek** recorded the 8 pathspec directories verbatim as its scope files\n134:   (`R/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-config.json`). It took the label's paths as the file list and\n135:   did not expand the range.\n136: - Both are \"valid\" under `scopeInsideTouchedFiles`, because a directory entry contains every file\n137:   under it. The relevance check is therefore much looser on deepseek, which could admit a sub-target\n138:   for a file the range never touched.\n139: - Root cause: `step_scope_discovery` has no commit-range branch (`deep-review.yaml:815-820`), so\n140:   each model improvises.\n141: - Opus raised this gap on its own as a depth-2 frontier proposal at its first iteration:\n142:   `F-2-007`, under F-1-002, asking \"Does any workflow step give a commit-range review target its\n143:   touched files\" (`R/lineages/opus/frontier-nodes.jsonl`).\n144: - Timing: opus landed 2 iterations in about 5 minutes. Each state row carries\n145:   `durationMs: 300000`, which looks like a placeholder value rather than a measured one. Deepseek\n146:   had written its config and dashboard but no iteration yet.\n147: - Liveness: the stall watchdog did not fire on opus, even though `--output-format text` streams\n148:   nothing. The artifact poller counts lineage writes as progress (`fanout-run.cjs:2219-2234`), and\n149:   the ledger shows a `progress` heartbeat every 60 s for both lineages.\n150: \n151: ### P2. The deepseek lineage died at +10 min on provider quota, after one iteration\n152: \n153: - `R/orchestration-status.log` line 23: `failed`, `failure_class: quota`, `retry_verdict: fatal`,\n154:   `terminal: true`, `duration_ms: 596027`.\n155: - The provider body said: \"OpenCode Go monthly usage limit reached ... resets in 13d 13h\"\n156:   (HTTP 429, `retryAfterMs: 1171152000`). See the tail of `R/lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out`.\n157: - Good: the runner classified the error correctly and did not burn retries on a 429 with a 13-day\n158:   reset.\n159: - Bad, as UX:\n160:   - Nothing pre-flights the provider quota. `preflightFanoutCapabilities` checks binaries only.\n161:   - The failure appears only in the ledger. The running fan-out process prints nothing to stderr\n162:     about a dead lineage, so an operator watching the terminal sees no signal for the rest of the\n163:     run.\n164:   - A 2-lineage review silently becomes a 1-lineage review. The merge will report whatever it\n165:     reports.\n166: - Cost data: opencode-go JSON carried `\"cost\":0` on every `step_finish` (the subscription plan), and\n167:   token counts are present. The claude lineage, with `--output-format text`, carries no token or\n168:   cost data at all.\n169: - Recovery decision (my judgment call, recorded):\n170:   - The same model is served by LLM Gateway as `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`. That id is\n171:     the runner's own `OPENCODE_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`fanout-run.cjs:2756`), and the presentation asset\n172:     names both ids as the same DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (`deep-review-presentation.txt:226`).\n173:   - The probe returned `42` and reported cost `0.000069834` (`D/probe/oc-probe.out`).\n174:   - Once opus settles, I re-dispatch only the `deepseek` label through `fanout-run.cjs` with\n175:     `--allow-single-lineage`, the same lineage directory and the new model. The lineage resumes its\n176:     stored session and frontier store.\n177:   - It is not done concurrently: two runners would share one `orchestration-status.log`, and\n178:     `markOrphanedLineages` reads that ledger at start.\n179: - Contract gap: there is no documented way to re-run one failed lineage of a fan-out. The only\n180:   route is the internal `--allow-single-lineage` flag, which the runner's own refusal text describes\n181:   as leaving the workflow.\n182: \n183: ### P3. The opus lineage stopped converged at run 15 of 24, in 28.5 min (18:36:58 to 19:05:31)\n184: \n185: - Timing:\n186:   - 14 iterations, about 1.4 to 4 min each. The `D/fanout.out` summary records `duration_ms: 1712943`.\n187:   - That is far below the 7 to 8 minutes per iteration that `review.md:100` warns about.\n188:   - `maxDurationMinutes` (120) never came into play.\n189: - Stop path:\n190:   - Stuck recovery fired twice: `stuckRecovery` events at runs 10 and 13.\n191:   - A `blocked_stop` at run 14 came from `graphlessFallbackGate`, reason\n192:     `add-cited-fallback-ledger-rows`.\n193:   - Then `terminal_gates` returned `stopReason: converged` at run 15.\n194:   - Then `synthesis_incomplete`, reason `synthesis_artifact_invariant_failed`, invariant\n195:     `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`.\n196:   - All of these are in `R/lineages/opus/deep-review-state.jsonl`.\n197: - Registry loss:\n198:   - The deltas hold 18 findings (3 P1, 15 P2). The registry holds 14 open (2 P1, 12 P2).\n199:   - `OPUS-REC-P1-003` and `OPUS-F006-P2-003` are missing.\n200:   - `OPUS-F004-P1-001` folded into `OPUS-F002-P2-002`, which the registry now shows as P1.\n201:   - The lineage flagged the loss itself, but the runner still marked the lineage `fulfilled`\n202:     (`D/fanout.out`).\n203: - Frontier behavior (`R/lineages/opus/frontier-nodes.jsonl`, the registry `frontier` block):\n204:   - F-1-002 and F-1-006 were answered with all four dimensions.\n205:   - F-1-004 (the command surface) was closed `exhausted/stuck` at run 10. Its node-bound passes\n206:     were correctness, security and traceability only. Its maintainability pass was never\n207:     dispatched.\n208:   - The stuck counter that closed it was built from two clean passes on *other* nodes: run 8 on\n209:     F-1-002, ratio 0, and run 9 on F-1-006, ratio 0.036. Both sit at or below the no-progress\n210:     cutoff, which is `0.5 x 0.10 = 0.05` (`convergence.cjs:757`, `:1387`).\n211:   - F-2-007 was admitted at run 1: one growth proposal, depth 2, under F-1-002. It got one pass\n212:     (correctness, run 12) and was closed `exhausted/stuck` at run 13. Run 12 found a new issue\n213:     but reported ratio 0.05, which counts as no-progress.\n214:   - So the expansive mode's \"do not stop while nodes are open\" promise is defeated by a stuck\n215:     counter that is lineage-wide rather than per node. The run converged with one depth-1 node a\n216:     dimension short and the depth-2 node three dimensions short, and `searchDebt` reads 0.\n217:   - The reviewer found this independently (OPUS-F004-P1-002, OPUS-REC-P1-003), from inside the run\n218:     it was reviewing.\n219: - The registry reports F-1-004's covered dimensions as all four, although no node-bound\n220:   maintainability pass ran. Run 13's recovery pass, not bound to a node, appears to be credited to\n221:   it. That is misleading on the dashboard.\n222: - Growth: 1 proposal admitted (F-2-007) against 9 available growth slots, and none pruned. Opus\n223:   proposed sparingly.\n224: - Writes outside `review/`: the runner's `metadata_refresh` rewrote the packet's\n225:   `description.json` at settle (`R/orchestration-status.log`, `metadata_refresh_ok`\n226:   `generate-description.js`). That is expected per `metadataRefreshRequested`, but it is a write\n227:   outside the artifact dir that the operator did not ask for.\n228: \n229: ### P4. Provider exhaustion: how the runner handled it\n230: \n231: All times are UTC. The ledger writes UTC, and file mtimes show local time (UTC+1), which misleads\n232: when the two are read side by side.\n233: \n234: - **Timeline**\n235:   - 18:37:03: deepseek spawned on `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max`, as pid 60602.\n236:   - 18:37:21: the first opencode JSON event.\n237:   - The lineage worked for about 9.5 minutes. It wrote its config, strategy, dashboard and\n238:     `iteration-001.md`: 1 iteration, 292 JSON events.\n239:   - 18:46:52.767: opencode emitted a single `{\"type\":\"error\"}` event, `provider.go-limit`, HTTP 429:\n240:     \"OpenCode Go monthly usage limit reached ... resets in 13d 13h\". The quota ran out\n241:     *mid-run*, not at launch.\n242:   - 18:46:54.538: the runner recorded `failed` with `failure_class: quota`,\n243:     `retry_verdict: fatal`, `retryable: false` and `terminal: true`, about **1.8 s** after the error\n244:     event.\n245: - **Did it fail loud or hang? It failed loud in the ledger, fast and correctly.**\n246:   - opencode exited with code 1 straight away. There was no hang and no stall-watchdog involvement.\n247:   - The runner's failure classifier read the provider body, and with no retries the remaining\n248:     13-day reset was not wasted.\n249:   - The opus lineage kept running unaffected, as `gauges.failed` went to 1.\n250: - **Did the operator see it? Not unless they read the ledger.**\n251:   - `fanout-run.cjs` wrote nothing to stderr about the failure. `D/fanout.err` holds only the two\n252:     budget lines and the `--auto` warning.\n253:   - It kept printing `progress` heartbeats for opus only.\n254:   - The conductor (me) noticed at the next poll, 18:59, about **12 minutes after the failure**.\n255:   - The final JSON on stdout and the process exit code 2 (`status: partial`) did carry it, but only\n256:     once the whole fan-out ended, 18 minutes later.\n257: - **Pre-flight**: `preflightFanoutCapabilities` checks binaries, not provider quota. A launch-time\n258:   probe would not have caught this case anyway, because the quota ran out after the launch.\n259: - **Recovery cost**:\n260:   - There is no documented single-lineage rerun.\n261:   - I used `fanout-run.cjs --allow-single-lineage` with a one-entry matrix\n262:     (`R/fanout-config-recovery.json`) under the same `--base-artifact-dir` and the same label\n263:     `deepseek`. It reuses `lineages/deepseek/`, so the stored session id and frontier store\n264:     carry over.\n265:   - It was launched 19:06:04, after opus settled, as runner pid 57919, lineage pid 59596, watchdog\n266:     pid 57920 at 180 min.\n267:   - The built command, confirmed from the live process and `lineages/deepseek/invocation-metadata.json`:\n268:     `opencode run --standalone -m llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max --format json --auto`,\n269:     model `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, `reasoningEffort: max`.\n270:   - Route (a) was accepted: `cli-opencode` takes the `llmgateway/` prefix. Vibe was not needed.\n271: - **Deviation**: the coordinator later asked for a dry run before the rerun. The rerun was already\n272:   live by then, launched on my own judgment at 19:06. The checks it did get were the provider probe\n273:   (`D/probe/oc-probe.out`, prints `42`) and the live process arguments, not a pre-launch preview.\n274:   The workflow's dry run cannot show fan-out lineage commands anyway (F1).\n275: - **The lineage clock**: the resumed lineage keeps its `createdAt` of 18:41:16 and its\n276:   `maxDurationMinutes` of 120. Its duration stop therefore falls around 20:41 UTC, so the recovery\n277:   has about 95 minutes, not 120. The 9.5 minutes lost to the quota failure and the 19 minutes spent\n278:   waiting for opus both count against it.\n279: \n280: ### P5. The deepseek recovery is running (status 19:17 UTC)\n281: \n282: - The resume worked as hoped:\n283:   - Iteration 1 from the dead attempt was kept: F-1-003 correctness, timestamp 18:45:15.\n284:   - The recovery continued at iteration 2 (F-1-005 correctness, 19:12:21) and iteration 3\n285:     (F-1-007 correctness, 19:16:25), in the same `lineages/deepseek/` dir and node store.\n286: - Pace is about 4 to 5 min per iteration, against opus's 1.4 to 4 min. Opus finished its whole\n287:   14-iteration lineage in less time than deepseek needs for about 6 iterations.\n288: - Lineage differences in artifact shape:\n289:   - Opus appended an `active` row to `frontier-nodes.jsonl` on every node visit; 17 rows for 4\n290:     nodes.\n291:   - Deepseek appends none. Its store still holds only the 3 `open` seed rows, so node activity is\n292:     visible only through the reducer's registry projection, not the store.\n293:   - Deepseek's state rows carry `timestamp` values rounded to whole seconds (`...:21.000Z`).\n294:     Opus's carry milliseconds.\n295:   - Opus's `durationMs` was a flat 300000 on every row.\n296: \n297: ### P6. The deepseek recovery finished, but 9 of its 12 iterations look rubber-stamped\n298: \n299: - The runner finished 19:25:56 with `status: ok`, the lineage `fulfilled` and exit 0, after 19.9 min\n300:   (`D/rec.out`).\n301: - On paper, the lineage did 12 iterations and answered all 3 nodes (F-1-003, F-1-005 and F-1-007)\n302:   with all four dimensions each.\n303: - The shape says otherwise:\n304:   - Iterations 4 to 12 were written 20 to 60 s apart (iteration file mtimes 19:18:05 to 19:23:38\n305:     UTC).\n306:   - Each record claims a whole-minute timestamp (19:18:00, 19:19:00 ... 19:26:00).\n307:   - Iteration 12's record says 19:26:00, *after* the lineage's own `synthesis_incomplete` row at\n308:     19:25:13 and after the runner recorded the lineage complete at 19:25:56.\n309:   - Six of the nine passes report 0 findings. The narratives shrink from about 1,300 words\n310:     (iterations 1 to 3) to 570 to 820 words.\n311: - The lineage never ran the stop gates. Its state log has no `terminal_gates`, `stuckRecovery` or\n312:   `blocked_stop` row, even though passes 6 to 11 all had ratio 0, which would have tripped stuck\n313:   recovery twice under opus's rules. It ends straight on `synthesis_incomplete` with\n314:   `stopReason: converged`.\n315: - The runner's timestamp-window check (`fanout-run.cjs`, `timestamp_anomaly` in `D/rec.out`)\n316:   flagged only the 2 legitimate pre-resume rows (`before_window`). It missed the future-stamped row,\n317:   which sits inside its 120 s tolerance.\n318: - **The biggest behavioral gap between the two lineages:**\n319:   - Opus executed the workflow's per-iteration convergence and stop steps: stuck recovery, the\n320:     blocked stop and the legal terminal gates.\n321:   - Deepseek, given the same prompt, skipped them and stamped out the remaining dimension passes.\n322:   - The fan-out runner accepted both as `fulfilled`. Nothing in the completion contract checks that\n323:     a CLI lineage ran the stop gates before it claims `converged`.\n324: \n325: ### P7. Merge, verdict and closeout on the fan-out root\n326: \n327: - `fanout-merge.cjs` returned `merged_verdict: CONDITIONAL`, P0 0, P1 4, P2 18, `search_debt: 0`,\n328:   and `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`).\n329: - The counts are an exact sum of the two lineage registries (opus 2/12, deepseek 2/6). No\n330:   cross-lineage dedupe happened. That is correct here, because no two findings named the same\n331:   file:line.\n332: - `review-verdict.cjs` gave CONDITIONAL (`D/verdict.out`).\n333: - `synthesis-closeout.cjs` on the root wrote a `synthesis_incomplete` row with\n334:   `structured_state_findings_partially_reflected_in_registry`, 26 against 22, and `runId: \"review\"`.\n335:   - The runId is the artifact folder name, because a fan-out root has no config\n336:     (`synthesis-closeout.cjs:280-289`).\n337:   - Both lineages wrote the same invariant failure.\n338: - **Correction to P3: the registry lost nothing.** All 4 \"missing\" ids, 3 from opus and 1 from\n339:   deepseek, were recorded as *refinements* of an earlier finding. The registry keeps the earlier id,\n340:   takes the refined title and severity, and logs the transition\n341:   `\"Refinement of an earlier finding\"`. Examples:\n342:   - `OPUS-REC-P1-003` into `OPUS-F004-P1-002`.\n343:   - `OPUS-F004-P1-001` into `OPUS-F002-P2-002`, raised to P1.\n344:   - `R2-P2-001` into `R1-P2-002`.\n345: - So the invariant check is a **false alarm**: it compares delta ids against registry ids and does\n346:   not understand refinements. The real friction is twofold:\n347:   - Every run that refines a finding reports \"synthesis incomplete\".\n348:   - A refined finding keeps an id that names the wrong iteration and severity:\n349:     `OPUS-F002-P2-002` is a P1 whose title came from iteration 7.\n350: - `step_update_config_status` cannot run on a fan-out root, because there is no root config to mark\n351:   complete. `step_emit_resource_map` and `step_refresh_completed_dashboard` both skip on fan-out, so\n352:   the root has **no dashboard at all**. The operator gets two lineage dashboards, the attribution\n353:   file and the report.\n354: \n355: ### P8. Save phase\n356: \n357: - `generate-context.js` without `--full-auto` is documented as plan-only (`deep-review.yaml:2556`\n358:   requirements).\n359: - It still rewrote the packet's `description.json`: it bumped `memorySequence` to 4, appended a\n360:   `memoryNameHistory` entry and set `lastUpdated` to 19:28:51.\n361: - The fan-out runner's settle-time `metadata_refresh` had already replaced that file's\n362:   `description` and `keywords` with text auto-extracted from `spec.md` (\"The deep-research and\n363:   deep-review loops converge on the three to five questions ...\").\n364: - Both writes were outside `review/`, and neither was asked for. I restored the file to HEAD\n365:   (`git restore`), because the tree was clean at the start and the operator wants no doc edits.\n366: - **Deviation from the workflow:** I skipped `step_generate_context --full-auto`, the continuity\n367:   write into packet docs, for the same reason.\n368: \n369: ### P9. Lineage differences, side by side\n370: \n371: | Aspect | opus (cli-claude-code, claude-opus-5-5, medium) | deepseek (cli-opencode) |\n372: |---|---|---|\n373: | Launch | needed `sandboxMode: danger-full-access`. Default `acceptEdits` cannot run Bash in `-p` mode (F2) | default resolves to `--auto` with a FATAL WARN banner |\n374: | Provider | ran clean | opencode-go hit its monthly quota after 9.5 min; relaunched on llmgateway |\n375: | Wall clock | 28.5 min for 14 iterations | 9.9 min (1 iteration) + 19.9 min (11 iterations) |\n376: | Per-iteration time | 1.4 to 4 min, evenly spread | 4 to 9 min for real passes, then 20 to 60 s rubber stamps |\n377: | Scope discovery | 232 touched files | 8 pathspec directories |\n378: | Node store rows | appends `active` per visit (17 rows) | none past the seed (3 rows) |\n379: | Stop machinery | stuck x2, blocked stop, terminal gates | none recorded |\n380: | Growth proposals | 1 (F-2-007) | 0 |\n381: | Findings | 18 deltas, 14 registry (2 P1) | 9 deltas, 8 registry (2 P1) |\n382: | Timestamps | millisecond precision; `durationMs` a flat 300000 | whole seconds or whole minutes, one in the future |\n383: | Cost data | none (text output) | token counts per step; cost 0 on opencode-go, real cost on llmgateway |\n384: \n385: ### P10. Report and dashboard clarity\n386: \n387: - With no root dashboard and no root config, the per-run \"what happened\" view of a fan-out review\n388:   is scattered across:\n389:   - `orchestration-status.log` (UTC, one heartbeat per lineage per minute)\n390:   - two lineage dashboards\n391:   - `fanout-attribution.md`\n392:   - the merged registry\n393: - `fanout-attribution.md` is the closest thing to a summary.\n394: - The runner's stdout JSON is the only place the final per-lineage status appears, and it is\n395:   machine-shaped.\n396: - The duration estimate in `review.md:100` (\"seven to eight minutes an iteration\") was wrong in\n397:   both directions: opus averaged about 2 minutes, and deepseek's real passes took 4 to 9.\n398: \n399: ## Stop reasons and totals\n400: \n401: - **opus**: `converged` (terminal gates at run 15), 14 iterations, 28.5 min.\n402: - **deepseek**:\n403:   - First attempt: `quota` failure, 1 iteration, 9.9 min.\n404:   - Recovery: `converged`, recorded only in `synthesis_incomplete` with no terminal gates, 11 more\n405:     iterations, 19.9 min.\n406: - **Fan-out wall clock**: 18:36:58 to 19:25:56, 49 min including the 30 s handover between runs.\n407:   Root synthesis followed until 19:28.\n408: - `maxDurationMinutes` (120) and the 180-min watchdogs never fired.\n409: \n410: ## Commit\n411: \n412: Commit `a424fb6cd8a` on `worktrees/455-expansive-depth-integration` stages the whole artifact dir, as `step_stage_artifact_dir` does:\n413: `review/` (root, both lineages and the raw lineage logs) plus `review-archive/20261119T183614Z/`.\n414: The tree was clean after the commit. All captured PIDs (57348, 57349, 57919, 57920) had exited by then; none was killed.\n415: \n416: ## Late checks\n417: \n418: - **F2 re-checked from the integration root**, where Claude Code also loads the repo's\n419:   `.claude/settings.json`. That file has `allow: []`. The same refusal came back with exit 0\n420:   (`D/probe/claude-probe3.out`). F2 stands as a contract bug rather than a probe artifact.\n421: - **R2-P1-001 is reachable**: `thought` is an allowed review status (`.skilled/agents/deep-review.md:236`).\n422: - **R3-P1-001**: no decision in `011-review-frontier-mode/decision-record.md` supersedes REQ-007's\n423:   pivot admission. It is a live spec/YAML contradiction, so the fix is a Logic-Sync choice: amend\n424:   the spec or implement the admission.\n425: - **The resumed lineage overwrote the failed attempt's raw log**:\n426:   - The committed `lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out` holds one session, the llmgateway\n427:     recovery. The opencode-go attempt and its 429 body survive only in the ledger's `failed` row.\n428:   - Sums for the committed log: 188 steps, 603,093 input, 80,386 output, 96,064 reasoning,\n429:     51,752,832 cache-read tokens, cost $0.4202.\n430:   - The opus lineage log holds only its 3.7 KB final text answer, so it carries no token data.\n431: - **Secrets scan** of both committed lineage logs found no email address or key. The 429 body that\n432:   carries the OpenCode workspace id and console URL lives in the ledger\n433:   (`review/orchestration-status.log`), which is committed. That is flagged only.\n434: - **Correction to the coordinator's framing** (\"the registry lost 2 and folded 1\"): every one of the\n435:   4 missing ids is a refinement kept under an earlier id. One side effect is real: a refinement\n436:   keeps the earlier file:line. `OPUS-F004-P1-001`'s location, `deep-review.yaml:815`, now survives\n437:   only as `frontier-admit.cjs:618`. The real \"fulfilled\" problem is P6: deepseek was accepted with\n438:   no stop-gate rows at all.\n439: - **Coverage caveat**: deepseek's security, traceability and maintainability passes on fan-out,\n440:   reducers and pivot (F-1-003, F-1-005, F-1-007) were the 20 to 60 s stamps. Zero P0 on those\n441:   surfaces means *not examined*, not clean."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-review-gen2.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795179516858,"end":1795179516987}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795179518436,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f90999e40013N4v6hXPyh2vpu","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9098ee500119ZG0Z5o796uCc","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"6b5b21db7387e30aca41f4b5e12bfa451c748acb","cost":0.000551832,"tokens":{"input":563,"output":70,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":95808,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795179519938,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f9099fc2001hB7HWB17wnseJU","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f90999ea001IYhHrtMtCt9Oef","type":"step-start","snapshot":"6b5b21db7387e30aca41f4b5e12bfa451c748acb"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179520038,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f9099fc5002sZlqzdvTVk19Fd","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f90999ea001IYhHrtMtCt9Oef","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9af00a5e60ce6d5f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-research-gen3.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-research-gen3.md, lines 1-311\n1: # Dogfood log: /deep:research --depth-mode=expansive, fan-out opus + deepseek\n2: \n3: > Kept from the conductor's session scratchpad. Paths under `D/` named the conductor's scratch evidence, which was not kept; the packet paths (`R/`, `SPEC/`) still resolve.\n4: \n5: Run on the integration worktree at `d4420e9510d` (clean at start). Spec folder\n6: `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode` (`SPEC`).\n7: `D` below means this scratch directory (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/`), `R` the packet's\n8: `research/` directory. The previous review dogfood is `scratchpad/dogfood/dogfood-log.md` (`PREV`).\n9: The conductor followed `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md` and `deep-research.yaml` step by step\n10: under `:auto`; deviations are named where they happen.\n11: \n12: ## Setup and invocation\n13: \n14: Invocation (as the operator would type it):\n15: \n16: ```\n17: /deep:research:auto \"<D/research-topic.txt>\" --spec-folder=SPEC --restart --depth-mode=expansive \\\n18:   --executors='<D/fanout-config.json>' --concurrency=2\n19: ```\n20: \n21: The matrix: opus = `cli-claude-code`, `claude-opus-5-5`, effort medium, configDir\n22: `~/.claude-account2`, `sandboxMode: danger-full-access`; deepseek = `cli-opencode`,\n23: `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, effort max. Budget left at default so the mode sizes itself.\n24: \n25: ### S1. The archive folder is `research_archive/`, not `research-archive/`\n26: \n27: - `resolveArtifactRoot(SPEC, 'research')` returns `artifactArchiveRoot: SPEC/research_archive`\n28:   (underscore). Review uses `review-archive` (hyphen). The brief said `research-archive/`.\n29: - I followed the resolver, because the YAML archives to `{state_paths.archive_root}`\n30:   (`deep-research.yaml:235`, `:359-366`). `research_archive/20261117T103614Z` (generation 1) already\n31:   lives there.\n32: - Friction: the two sibling loops spell their archive folder differently. An operator who looks for\n33:   `research-archive/` after a review run finds nothing.\n34: \n35: ### S2. The dry-run preview works and shows what it promised, except the topic\n36: \n37: - `step_fanout_dry_run_preview` (`deep-research.yaml:278-313`) ran `fanout-run.cjs --preview`\n38:   (`D/preview.out`, `D/preview.err`, exit 0). It wrote nothing (`git status` empty after).\n39: - **Confirmed from the preview**: opus `claude -p <prompt:digest> --model claude-opus-5-5\n40:   --permission-mode bypassPermissions --output-format text --effort medium`, `config_dir\n41:   ~/.claude-account2`, sandbox `danger-full-access`. Deepseek `opencode run --standalone -m\n42:   llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max --format json --auto <prompt:digest>`, effort max.\n43: - **Not confirmable from the preview**: the topic text. Every prompt is a digest. I rendered the\n44:   prompts read-only through the exported `buildLoopPrompt` (`D/render-prompt.cjs`): the topic is in\n45:   both prompts verbatim (`D/prompt-opus.txt` 46,309 chars, `D/prompt-deepseek.txt` 46,552 chars).\n46:   A `--preview-prompt` or a printed topic digest beside the topic file's digest would close this.\n47: - Preview oddities:\n48:   - The opencode entry's `effective_config.permissionMode` reads `acceptEdits`. That is the Claude\n49:     permission resolution passed through, although opencode has no permission flag. Claude, Devin\n50:     and dsh each pass their own `--permission-mode` values (`fanout-run.cjs:2582`, `:3026-3030`,\n51:     `:3316`).\n52:   - `FATAL WARN: lineage deepseek runs with --auto ...` is printed for a warning that is not fatal\n53:     (`D/preview.err`). Same banner as `PREV` F-block.\n54:   - `aggregate_budget.upper_bound.estimated_cost_units` is 20 while each `per_lineage` entry says\n55:     `estimated_cost_units: 60`. The two numbers use different units of \"estimated\" with no label.\n56:   - The opencode entry shows `stdin: \"<input>\"` while the prompt digest also sits in argv, so it is\n57:     unclear which channel carries the prompt.\n58:   - Before the seed, both lineages show `iterations: 10` and \"got no seed share\", as the docs say\n59:     (`research.md:145`). Expected, but the stderr line \"2 lineages share 0 open seed nodes\" reads\n60:     like a fault on a dry run.\n61: - The `dry_run_halt` line (`D/dry-run-halt.jsonl`) was **written by me with `echo`**, from the\n62:   YAML's `default_halt_event` template. No script emits it: the halt hook is prose the conductor\n63:   executes (`deep-research.yaml:107`). So the dry run's \"halt\" is only as reliable as the conductor.\n64: \n65: ### S3. Budget sizing at the default\n66: \n67: - Six seeds dealt round-robin give each CLI lineage 3 nodes, and\n68:   `expansiveBudget` gives `min(24, max(10, 2 x 1 x (3 + 3 - 1))) = 10`\n69:   (`frontier-admit.cjs:469-476`), which equals the CLI floor. Any seed count from 1 to 6 gives\n70:   every CLI lineage exactly 10 here, so \"the mode sizes itself\" is a constant for a 2-lineage run.\n71: - Node cap is half the budget, 5 per lineage, so 2 growth slots past the 3 seeds.\n72: \n73: ## Restart, seed and spawn\n74: \n75: ### S4. `--restart` archived the old packet intact\n76: \n77: - `bind_prior_lineage` read generation 2, session `2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z` (`D/prior-lineage.json`).\n78: - `research/` moved to `SPEC/research_archive/20261120T011847Z/`. Every one of the 80 tracked\n79:   `research/` files exists there, and the generation-1 archive `research_archive/20261117T103614Z/`\n80:   is untouched (`git diff` empty on it).\n81: - As in `PREV` F5, the fan-out parent never runs `step_create_config`, so nothing records the new\n82:   generation (3) or its parent session. The lineage chain the restart promises does not exist on the\n83:   fan-out path. Not fixed since the review.\n84: \n85: ### S5. Seeds: 6 admitted, 0 pruned\n86: \n87: - I wrote `R/frontier-seed.json` (6 sub-questions, 226 to 368 characters, under the 500 cap) and ran\n88:   `frontier-admit.cjs seed ... --max-iterations-source default` (`D/seed.out`, `D/seed.err`):\n89:   `admitted F-1-001..F-1-006, pruned []`.\n90: - Seed quality: each seed is one of the topic's Q1-Q6, so they are good by construction. Research\n91:   admission checks only that `question`, `scope` and `evidence` are non-empty strings: the\n92:   prior-art seed's scope \"web sources on agentic deep-research ...\" passed the relevance check,\n93:   which shows that relevance is a shape check for research, not a scope check.\n94: - **Judgment call on order**: nodes are dealt round-robin in code-unit id order with opus first,\n95:   so I placed the web question (Q6, prior art) at F-1-005 to land on opus, whose `claude -p` has\n96:   web tools. The deal in `R/orchestration-status.log` confirmed opus = F-1-001, F-1-003, F-1-005\n97:   and deepseek = F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006. An operator who does not know the dealing rule cannot\n98:   steer a web-only question to a web-capable lineage.\n99: - `PREV` F6 is still open: the parent seed prints `budget after seed 16 iterations, 2 growth slots`\n100:   (the single-executor figure), while each lineage runs 10 (`D/fanout.err`). Here the growth figure\n101:   happens to match (cap 5 - 3 seeds = 2 per lineage), the iteration figure does not.\n102: \n103: ### S6. Spawn\n104: \n105: - Inputs written with the file-write tool to `R/fanout-research-topic.txt` and\n106:   `R/fanout-config.json`, as `step_fanout_spawn` says. Runner launched at 01:19:42 UTC with\n107:   `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` exported, through `D/launch.sh`.\n108: - Process tree: runner 39805 re-executes itself as a `node --import ...` child 39812, which owns the\n109:   lineage processes opus 44925 and deepseek 44931 (`D/captured.pids`). A watchdog that kills \"the\n110:   runner PID\" and its direct children does not reach the lineage CLIs; my watchdog kills 39805 and\n111:   39812, and I would kill the two lineage PIDs by hand.\n112: - The per-lineage budget lines are right: `lineage opus budget 10 iterations, derived from its seed\n113:   share` (`D/fanout.err`).\n114: \n115: ### S7. Q5b checked independently before the lineages answer it\n116: \n117: - I ran the shipped `checkLineageCompletion` (`lineage-timestamp-window.ts:183`) with the research\n118:   terminal set over all 380 committed research lineage state logs, with the widest window so only\n119:   presence and order are judged (`D/check-completion.mjs`, `D/completion-check.txt`).\n120: - Result: 282 complete, 80 `no_terminal_event`, 10 `stale_terminal_event` (terminal row with no\n121:   parseable stamp), 8 `no_iteration_records`. 84 of the 98 failures have a `research.md` on disk,\n122:   and 32 have `status: complete` in their config.\n123: - The 12 newest committed lineages (2026-11-15/16) all pass. The operator's \"3 of 12\" is a sample\n124:   I could not reproduce; across the corpus the miss rate is 26%.\n125: \n126: ## Run progress\n127: \n128: ### P1. Both lineages ran clean on the first attempt (runner exit 0, `status: ok`)\n129: \n130: - Runner 01:19:43 to 01:39:52 UTC, **20.1 min** (`D/fanout.out`, `R/orchestration-status.log`).\n131: - **deepseek** (cli-opencode, `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max`): 10 iterations,\n132:   01:19:43 to 01:33:28, **13.7 min**, stop `maxIterationsReached` (`synthesis_complete` row at\n133:   01:32:00). Passes took 33 s to 98 s (iteration file mtimes 02:22:49 to 02:30:50 local).\n134: - **opus** (cli-claude-code, `claude-opus-5-5`, medium, `bypassPermissions`): 5 iterations,\n135:   01:19:43 to 01:39:52, **20.1 min**, stop `converged` (`synthesis_complete` at 01:37:08). Passes\n136:   took 2 to 5 min.\n137: - Setup inside each lineage (spawn to first state row): opus 1.3 min to its config row and 6.3 min\n138:   to iteration 1; deepseek 1.7 min to config and 3.3 min to iteration 1. That is far below the\n139:   \"8-11 minute setup\" the topic quotes.\n140: - No provider failure and no retry. Cost: deepseek's opencode JSON log\n141:   (`R/lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out`) sums to **$0.326** over 164 steps (482,143 input,\n142:   76,769 output, 36,774 reasoning, 34.7 M cache-read tokens; tools: 121 shell, 37 write, 32 read,\n143:   4 webfetch, 4 edit), about $0.033 per iteration. Opus's `--output-format text` log is its 3.8 KB\n144:   final answer and carries no token or cost data, as in `PREV` P9.\n145: \n146: ### P2. Pass quality: deepseek did real work this time, but its ratio is a constant\n147: \n148: - Unlike `PREV` P6 (20-60 s rubber stamps), every deepseek pass cites 11 to 22 distinct file:line\n149:   locations and runs 636 to 1,126 words (`R/lineages/deepseek/iterations/`).\n150: - But every deepseek iteration reports `newInfoRatio: 1` (`R/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-state.jsonl`),\n151:   10 of 10. Opus's ratios fall 0.93, 0.88, 0.75, 0.83, 0.55. A self-reported ratio that never\n152:   moves cannot drive convergence, so deepseek could only ever stop on the iteration cap.\n153: \n154: ### P3. Frontier growth (admitted and pruned, and why)\n155: \n156: - **opus**: 0 growth proposals. Each seed was marked answered after one pass, then one revisit of\n157:   F-1-001 and one blocked-stop recovery pass.\n158: - **deepseek**: 7 proposals. 2 admitted at depth 2 under F-1-002 (F-2-007 partial-run summary,\n159:   F-2-008 per-node dashboard spend). 5 pruned with reason `fanout` (F-2-009 to F-2-013 under F-1-004\n160:   and F-1-006): the lineage node cap is 5 (half its 10-iteration budget), and 3 seeds + 2 growth\n161:   filled it at iteration 1. The pruned ones were good questions (for example F-2-012 \"measured setup\n162:   time per executor kind\"). The cap, not relevance, decided what the run studied.\n163: - The prune reason `fanout` names the run-wide node cap as well as the per-parent child cap\n164:   (`frontier-admit.cjs:774-781`), so the store cannot tell the operator which cap bit.\n165: - F-1-006 (cost and latency) closed `exhausted/budget` in the reducer's projection after one\n166:   pass: the depth-1 band (50% of 10 = 5 visits) was spent across the three seeds.\n167: \n168: ### P4. Node store and registry disagree on every node\n169: \n170: - After the run, `R/lineages/*/frontier-nodes.jsonl` shows every seed `open`, and no closes at all.\n171: - The reducer projection in each lineage's `findings-registry.json` says opus F-1-001, F-1-003 and\n172:   F-1-005 are `answered`, and deepseek's F-1-002, F-1-004, F-2-007 and F-2-008 `answered`, F-1-006\n173:   `exhausted/budget`.\n174: - In research the only close the workflow writes to the store is the stuck close\n175:   (`deep-research.yaml:1528`). Answered and budget states live only in the reducer's projection, so\n176:   the file named \"the node store\" is stale for every node that finished normally. The frontier veto\n177:   reads the projection (`convergence.cjs:1559`, `:1749`), so behavior is right; the store misleads.\n178: - This also explains why opus could stop `converged` at iteration 5 while its store shows three open\n179:   nodes: the projection had none open, so the `frontierOpen` veto (`convergence.cjs:1206-1218`)\n180:   correctly did not fire.\n181: \n182: ### P5. Deepseek left its partition after its frontier drained\n183: \n184: - Iterations 1-7 worked deepseek's own nodes. Iterations 8, 9 and 10 took their focus straight from\n185:   the topic: \"Q1 restraint\", \"Q5 design questions\", \"Q6 prior art\". Those are opus's F-1-001,\n186:   F-1-003 and F-1-005.\n187: - Cause: once the projection holds no open node, Next Focus falls back to the topic text, and the\n188:   topic names all six questions. The partition only bounds the frontier, not the topic.\n189: - `fanout-merge.cjs` reported `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`): the guard\n190:   checks node ids, so topic-driven work on another lineage's question is invisible to it.\n191: - Effect: Q1, Q5 and Q6 got a second, cheaper view. Useful for cross-checking, but it is unbudgeted\n192:   duplicate work. Deepseek's prior-art pass made 4 `webfetch` calls and cites 4 URLs (Anthropic's\n193:   multi-agent research post, LangChain open_deep_research, two arXiv papers); opus's cites 15.\n194: \n195: ### P6. Opus stopped converged after a blocked stop\n196: \n197: - Iteration 5 is a `blocked_stop` recovery: `source_diversity_guard`, `evidence_depth_guard` and\n198:   `uncovered_questions` blocked the stop although all three nodes were answered\n199:   (`R/lineages/opus/iterations/iteration-005.md`). Opus traced the cause itself: the graph guards\n200:   read only the optional `graphEvents` (`iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:122`), not the mandatory finding\n201:   rows. This costs one recovery iteration per lineage that follows the mandatory contract.\n202: - The `blocked_stop` row carries `stopReason: \"legacy-blocked-stop\"` and a whole-second stamp\n203:   (`01:34:29.000Z`), while opus's iteration rows carry milliseconds.\n204: - Deepseek recorded no `blocked_stop`, `stuckRecovery` or any convergence row: its ratio of 1 never\n205:   reached a stop candidate, so the guards never ran.\n206: \n207: ## Synthesis on the fan-out root\n208: \n209: ### Y1. `step_fanout_merge` worked\n210: \n211: - `fanout-merge.cjs --loop-type research` exit 0, 2 lineages, 192 key findings,\n212:   `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`). The partition guard missed P5's topic\n213:   drift, as noted.\n214: - `fanout-attribution.md` lists opus \"Convergence 0.55\" and deepseek \"1\": the last ratio, labeled\n215:   as convergence.\n216: \n217: ### Y2. `step_emit_resource_map` failed on the fan-out root: no root config\n218: \n219: - The `if_present` command exited 3 with `ENOENT ... research/deep-research-config.json`\n220:   (`D/resmap.err`), because `emitFanoutResourceMap` requires a root config\n221:   (`reduce-state.cjs:1816-1819`) and the fan-out path writes none.\n222: - The `:auto` setup is supposed to persist the config (`research.md:88`). But under `--restart`,\n223:   `step_apply_lifecycle_request` would then archive that fresh config with the old packet, and\n224:   `bind_prior_lineage` would read the new session as the \"prior\" one. **This is a contract\n225:   contradiction.** Across the corpus, 104 of 192 committed fan-out research roots have neither a root\n226:   config nor a resource map.\n227: - **Judgment call:** I wrote the root config late, from the skill's template\n228:   (`deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json`). It holds generation 3, the parent session\n229:   `2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z`, `lineageMode: restart` and the fan-out matrix. The rerun then\n230:   emitted `R/resource-map.md` from 15 delta files (`D/resmap2.out`).\n231: - Both lineages hit the lineage-side twin of this defect: the single-loop `if_absent` command\n232:   (`deep-research.yaml:2155`) carries no `{reducer_artifact_arg}`. Deepseek's map failed with\n233:   ENOENT; opus added `--artifact-dir` by hand.\n234: \n235: ### Y3. `step_compile_research`, closeout and config status\n236: \n237: - I wrote `R/research.md` from both lineage syntheses and iterations.\n238: - `step_convergence_report` ran as written. The closeout emitted\n239:   `deep_research.synthesis_complete` (`totalIterations: 15`) and the gateway appended it with a\n240:   receipt (`D/closeout.out`). The root row carries `lineageId` = the *prior* session\n241:   (`2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z`), apparently taken from `parentSessionId`. That looks like a field\n242:   mix-up worth checking.\n243: - `step_update_config_status` set the late root config to `complete`.\n244: - The dashboard refresh and the terminal heartbeat skip on fan-out by design, so the root has **no\n245:   dashboard**, as in `PREV` P7.\n246: \n247: ### Y4. Deviations from the workflow (recorded)\n248: \n249: - I skipped `step_writeback_spec_findings` and its validation (they edit `SPEC/spec.md`), and\n250:   `phase_save --full-auto` (it writes continuity into packet docs). The brief is report-only with a\n251:   clean tree.\n252: - I restored the settle-time metadata refresh's rewrite of `SPEC/description.json` **and**\n253:   `SPEC/graph-metadata.json` (176-line diff in `D/metadata-refresh.diff`).\n254: \n255: ## Did the fixes since the review behave live?\n256: \n257: | Fix | Live result |\n258: |-----|-------------|\n259: | Fatal-failure stderr line (`f2de4f588c5`) | **Not exercised.** No lineage failed, so no terminal `failed` event fired. The code path is at `fanout-run.cjs:4185-4196`. |\n260: | Completion check (`a6c1332a331`, `1ea09919553`) | **Behaved, but it is weak for research.** Both lineages passed on `synthesis_complete`. Research's terminal set accepts any synthesis row, including `synthesis_incomplete` (`fanout-run.cjs:1248-1251`). Deepseek wrote no convergence or stop-gate row at all and still passed, the same gap `PREV` P6 named for review, which review closed with `terminal_gates`. |\n261: | Dry-run preview (`30c88ac2e2a`, `99a12d54838`, `377055592a5`) | **Worked.** It confirmed model, effort, sandbox, permission and config dir per lineage and wrote nothing. The topic text is not shown (digest only), so I confirmed it by rendering the prompt. Oddities are in S2. |\n262: | No `description.json` rewrite (`4c6a3a41f03`) | **Review only, by design.** The research fan-out still rewrote `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` at settle (`metadata_refresh_ok` x2 in `R/orchestration-status.log`), and the rewrite degraded both files. |\n263: | Log rotation on resume (`600d84b1677`) | **Not exercised.** There was no failed attempt and no resume. `fanout-lineage.out/.err` exist once per lineage, and no `.1` file exists. |\n264: | `--sandbox-mode` / `sandboxMode` for cli-claude-code | **Worked.** `bypassPermissions` in the preview and the live argv; opus ran Bash and recorded state. |\n265: | Per-lineage budget lines | **Worked**: `lineage opus budget 10 iterations, derived from its seed share`. |\n266: \n267: ## Lineage differences, side by side\n268: \n269: | Aspect | opus (cli-claude-code, claude-opus-5-5, medium) | deepseek (cli-opencode, llmgateway deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, max) |\n270: |---|---|---|\n271: | Wall clock | 20.1 min, 5 iterations | 13.7 min, 10 iterations |\n272: | Per iteration | 2 to 5 min | 0.5 to 1.6 min |\n273: | Stop | converged after 1 blocked stop (graph guards) | maxIterationsReached; no stop machinery ran |\n274: | Ratio | 0.93, 0.88, 0.75, 0.83, 0.55 | 1.0 on all 10 |\n275: | Growth proposals | 0 | 7 (2 admitted, 5 pruned by the node cap) |\n276: | Partition discipline | stayed on its 3 nodes | drifted into opus's Q1, Q5 and Q6 at iterations 8-10 |\n277: | Citations per pass | 46 in iteration 1 | 11 to 22 |\n278: | Web | 15 URLs | 4 URLs (4 `webfetch` calls) |\n279: | Resource map | worked around the missing `--artifact-dir` | failed with ENOENT and reported it |\n280: | Cost data | none (text output) | $0.326, 164 steps |\n281: | Workflow hygiene | self-reported one `sed -i` and one shell-redirect write against the prompt pack's rules | no self-report |\n282: \n283: ## Top frictions\n284: \n285: 1. The fan-out root has no config, so the resource map fails, the config status cannot be set and the\n286:    restart lineage chain is lost (Y2, S4).\n287: 2. The resource-map step drops the lineage artifact dir; both lineages hit it (Y2).\n288: 3. Expansive partitioning leaks: a drained lineage works other lineages' questions from the topic\n289:    (P5).\n290: 4. The node cap prunes growth at iteration 1, and the derived budget is a constant 10 for any\n291:    2-lineage research run (P3, S3).\n292: 5. The research completion check accepts a lineage that ran no stop machinery (fix table).\n293: 6. The node store says every node is open after a converged run (P4).\n294: 7. The research fan-out still rewrites and degrades packet metadata outside `research/` (Y4).\n295: 8. No root dashboard, and no per-lineage status in the summary (Y3).\n296: \n297: ## Commit\n298: \n299: - Commit `adade6c293e` (amended from `b37964ab6d5` to correct backlog rows 2 and 9) on `worktrees/455-expansive-depth-integration` (subject 71 characters, no\n300:   attribution lines). It holds 244 files: `research/` (root, both lineages, raw logs, the backlog)\n301:   and `research_archive/20261120T011847Z/` (69 renames plus files git did not pair).\n302: - The YAML's `step_stage_artifact_dir` command exited 1, because its exclude pathspec names the\n303:   gitignored `.legacy-projection-watermarks` and git refuses an ignored path even in an exclude.\n304:   Everything else staged; the step's `on_fail` is a warning.\n305: - The repo's pre-commit gate `[gate:spec-remint]` re-derived `SPEC/graph-metadata.json` and staged it\n306:   into the commit (`D/commit.out`). It correctly drops the archived root `research/` paths, but it\n307:   also drops the trigger phrases `depth-mode expansive` and `frontier veto`, the same loss as the\n308:   runner's settle-time refresh. `description.json` was not touched. I did not fight the hook.\n309: - The hook asked for no dsh mirror sync. The tree was clean after the commit. All captured PIDs\n310:   (39805, 39806, 39812, 44925 and 44931) had exited by themselves; none was killed, and the 180-minute\n311:   watchdog never fired.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-research-gen3.md, lines 1-311\n1: # Dogfood log: /deep:research --depth-mode=expansive, fan-out opus + deepseek\n2: \n3: > Kept from the conductor's session scratchpad. Paths under `D/` named the conductor's scratch evidence, which was not kept; the packet paths (`R/`, `SPEC/`) still resolve.\n4: \n5: Run on the integration worktree at `d4420e9510d` (clean at start). Spec folder\n6: `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode` (`SPEC`).\n7: `D` below means this scratch directory (`scratchpad/dogfood-research/`), `R` the packet's\n8: `research/` directory. The previous review dogfood is `scratchpad/dogfood/dogfood-log.md` (`PREV`).\n9: The conductor followed `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md` and `deep-research.yaml` step by step\n10: under `:auto`; deviations are named where they happen.\n11: \n12: ## Setup and invocation\n13: \n14: Invocation (as the operator would type it):\n15: \n16: ```\n17: /deep:research:auto \"<D/research-topic.txt>\" --spec-folder=SPEC --restart --depth-mode=expansive \\\n18:   --executors='<D/fanout-config.json>' --concurrency=2\n19: ```\n20: \n21: The matrix: opus = `cli-claude-code`, `claude-opus-5-5`, effort medium, configDir\n22: `~/.claude-account2`, `sandboxMode: danger-full-access`; deepseek = `cli-opencode`,\n23: `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`, effort max. Budget left at default so the mode sizes itself.\n24: \n25: ### S1. The archive folder is `research_archive/`, not `research-archive/`\n26: \n27: - `resolveArtifactRoot(SPEC, 'research')` returns `artifactArchiveRoot: SPEC/research_archive`\n28:   (underscore). Review uses `review-archive` (hyphen). The brief said `research-archive/`.\n29: - I followed the resolver, because the YAML archives to `{state_paths.archive_root}`\n30:   (`deep-research.yaml:235`, `:359-366`). `research_archive/20261117T103614Z` (generation 1) already\n31:   lives there.\n32: - Friction: the two sibling loops spell their archive folder differently. An operator who looks for\n33:   `research-archive/` after a review run finds nothing.\n34: \n35: ### S2. The dry-run preview works and shows what it promised, except the topic\n36: \n37: - `step_fanout_dry_run_preview` (`deep-research.yaml:278-313`) ran `fanout-run.cjs --preview`\n38:   (`D/preview.out`, `D/preview.err`, exit 0). It wrote nothing (`git status` empty after).\n39: - **Confirmed from the preview**: opus `claude -p <prompt:digest> --model claude-opus-5-5\n40:   --permission-mode bypassPermissions --output-format text --effort medium`, `config_dir\n41:   ~/.claude-account2`, sandbox `danger-full-access`. Deepseek `opencode run --standalone -m\n42:   llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max --format json --auto <prompt:digest>`, effort max.\n43: - **Not confirmable from the preview**: the topic text. Every prompt is a digest. I rendered the\n44:   prompts read-only through the exported `buildLoopPrompt` (`D/render-prompt.cjs`): the topic is in\n45:   both prompts verbatim (`D/prompt-opus.txt` 46,309 chars, `D/prompt-deepseek.txt` 46,552 chars).\n46:   A `--preview-prompt` or a printed topic digest beside the topic file's digest would close this.\n47: - Preview oddities:\n48:   - The opencode entry's `effective_config.permissionMode` reads `acceptEdits`. That is the Claude\n49:     permission resolution passed through, although opencode has no permission flag. Claude, Devin\n50:     and dsh each pass their own `--permission-mode` values (`fanout-run.cjs:2582`, `:3026-3030`,\n51:     `:3316`).\n52:   - `FATAL WARN: lineage deepseek runs with --auto ...` is printed for a warning that is not fatal\n53:     (`D/preview.err`). Same banner as `PREV` F-block.\n54:   - `aggregate_budget.upper_bound.estimated_cost_units` is 20 while each `per_lineage` entry says\n55:     `estimated_cost_units: 60`. The two numbers use different units of \"estimated\" with no label.\n56:   - The opencode entry shows `stdin: \"<input>\"` while the prompt digest also sits in argv, so it is\n57:     unclear which channel carries the prompt.\n58:   - Before the seed, both lineages show `iterations: 10` and \"got no seed share\", as the docs say\n59:     (`research.md:145`). Expected, but the stderr line \"2 lineages share 0 open seed nodes\" reads\n60:     like a fault on a dry run.\n61: - The `dry_run_halt` line (`D/dry-run-halt.jsonl`) was **written by me with `echo`**, from the\n62:   YAML's `default_halt_event` template. No script emits it: the halt hook is prose the conductor\n63:   executes (`deep-research.yaml:107`). So the dry run's \"halt\" is only as reliable as the conductor.\n64: \n65: ### S3. Budget sizing at the default\n66: \n67: - Six seeds dealt round-robin give each CLI lineage 3 nodes, and\n68:   `expansiveBudget` gives `min(24, max(10, 2 x 1 x (3 + 3 - 1))) = 10`\n69:   (`frontier-admit.cjs:469-476`), which equals the CLI floor. Any seed count from 1 to 6 gives\n70:   every CLI lineage exactly 10 here, so \"the mode sizes itself\" is a constant for a 2-lineage run.\n71: - Node cap is half the budget, 5 per lineage, so 2 growth slots past the 3 seeds.\n72: \n73: ## Restart, seed and spawn\n74: \n75: ### S4. `--restart` archived the old packet intact\n76: \n77: - `bind_prior_lineage` read generation 2, session `2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z` (`D/prior-lineage.json`).\n78: - `research/` moved to `SPEC/research_archive/20261120T011847Z/`. Every one of the 80 tracked\n79:   `research/` files exists there, and the generation-1 archive `research_archive/20261117T103614Z/`\n80:   is untouched (`git diff` empty on it).\n81: - As in `PREV` F5, the fan-out parent never runs `step_create_config`, so nothing records the new\n82:   generation (3) or its parent session. The lineage chain the restart promises does not exist on the\n83:   fan-out path. Not fixed since the review.\n84: \n85: ### S5. Seeds: 6 admitted, 0 pruned\n86: \n87: - I wrote `R/frontier-seed.json` (6 sub-questions, 226 to 368 characters, under the 500 cap) and ran\n88:   `frontier-admit.cjs seed ... --max-iterations-source default` (`D/seed.out`, `D/seed.err`):\n89:   `admitted F-1-001..F-1-006, pruned []`.\n90: - Seed quality: each seed is one of the topic's Q1-Q6, so they are good by construction. Research\n91:   admission checks only that `question`, `scope` and `evidence` are non-empty strings: the\n92:   prior-art seed's scope \"web sources on agentic deep-research ...\" passed the relevance check,\n93:   which shows that relevance is a shape check for research, not a scope check.\n94: - **Judgment call on order**: nodes are dealt round-robin in code-unit id order with opus first,\n95:   so I placed the web question (Q6, prior art) at F-1-005 to land on opus, whose `claude -p` has\n96:   web tools. The deal in `R/orchestration-status.log` confirmed opus = F-1-001, F-1-003, F-1-005\n97:   and deepseek = F-1-002, F-1-004, F-1-006. An operator who does not know the dealing rule cannot\n98:   steer a web-only question to a web-capable lineage.\n99: - `PREV` F6 is still open: the parent seed prints `budget after seed 16 iterations, 2 growth slots`\n100:   (the single-executor figure), while each lineage runs 10 (`D/fanout.err`). Here the growth figure\n101:   happens to match (cap 5 - 3 seeds = 2 per lineage), the iteration figure does not.\n102: \n103: ### S6. Spawn\n104: \n105: - Inputs written with the file-write tool to `R/fanout-research-topic.txt` and\n106:   `R/fanout-config.json`, as `step_fanout_spawn` says. Runner launched at 01:19:42 UTC with\n107:   `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` exported, through `D/launch.sh`.\n108: - Process tree: runner 39805 re-executes itself as a `node --import ...` child 39812, which owns the\n109:   lineage processes opus 44925 and deepseek 44931 (`D/captured.pids`). A watchdog that kills \"the\n110:   runner PID\" and its direct children does not reach the lineage CLIs; my watchdog kills 39805 and\n111:   39812, and I would kill the two lineage PIDs by hand.\n112: - The per-lineage budget lines are right: `lineage opus budget 10 iterations, derived from its seed\n113:   share` (`D/fanout.err`).\n114: \n115: ### S7. Q5b checked independently before the lineages answer it\n116: \n117: - I ran the shipped `checkLineageCompletion` (`lineage-timestamp-window.ts:183`) with the research\n118:   terminal set over all 380 committed research lineage state logs, with the widest window so only\n119:   presence and order are judged (`D/check-completion.mjs`, `D/completion-check.txt`).\n120: - Result: 282 complete, 80 `no_terminal_event`, 10 `stale_terminal_event` (terminal row with no\n121:   parseable stamp), 8 `no_iteration_records`. 84 of the 98 failures have a `research.md` on disk,\n122:   and 32 have `status: complete` in their config.\n123: - The 12 newest committed lineages (2026-11-15/16) all pass. The operator's \"3 of 12\" is a sample\n124:   I could not reproduce; across the corpus the miss rate is 26%.\n125: \n126: ## Run progress\n127: \n128: ### P1. Both lineages ran clean on the first attempt (runner exit 0, `status: ok`)\n129: \n130: - Runner 01:19:43 to 01:39:52 UTC, **20.1 min** (`D/fanout.out`, `R/orchestration-status.log`).\n131: - **deepseek** (cli-opencode, `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017#max`): 10 iterations,\n132:   01:19:43 to 01:33:28, **13.7 min**, stop `maxIterationsReached` (`synthesis_complete` row at\n133:   01:32:00). Passes took 33 s to 98 s (iteration file mtimes 02:22:49 to 02:30:50 local).\n134: - **opus** (cli-claude-code, `claude-opus-5-5`, medium, `bypassPermissions`): 5 iterations,\n135:   01:19:43 to 01:39:52, **20.1 min**, stop `converged` (`synthesis_complete` at 01:37:08). Passes\n136:   took 2 to 5 min.\n137: - Setup inside each lineage (spawn to first state row): opus 1.3 min to its config row and 6.3 min\n138:   to iteration 1; deepseek 1.7 min to config and 3.3 min to iteration 1. That is far below the\n139:   \"8-11 minute setup\" the topic quotes.\n140: - No provider failure and no retry. Cost: deepseek's opencode JSON log\n141:   (`R/lineages/deepseek/logs/fanout-lineage.out`) sums to **$0.326** over 164 steps (482,143 input,\n142:   76,769 output, 36,774 reasoning, 34.7 M cache-read tokens; tools: 121 shell, 37 write, 32 read,\n143:   4 webfetch, 4 edit), about $0.033 per iteration. Opus's `--output-format text` log is its 3.8 KB\n144:   final answer and carries no token or cost data, as in `PREV` P9.\n145: \n146: ### P2. Pass quality: deepseek did real work this time, but its ratio is a constant\n147: \n148: - Unlike `PREV` P6 (20-60 s rubber stamps), every deepseek pass cites 11 to 22 distinct file:line\n149:   locations and runs 636 to 1,126 words (`R/lineages/deepseek/iterations/`).\n150: - But every deepseek iteration reports `newInfoRatio: 1` (`R/lineages/deepseek/deep-research-state.jsonl`),\n151:   10 of 10. Opus's ratios fall 0.93, 0.88, 0.75, 0.83, 0.55. A self-reported ratio that never\n152:   moves cannot drive convergence, so deepseek could only ever stop on the iteration cap.\n153: \n154: ### P3. Frontier growth (admitted and pruned, and why)\n155: \n156: - **opus**: 0 growth proposals. Each seed was marked answered after one pass, then one revisit of\n157:   F-1-001 and one blocked-stop recovery pass.\n158: - **deepseek**: 7 proposals. 2 admitted at depth 2 under F-1-002 (F-2-007 partial-run summary,\n159:   F-2-008 per-node dashboard spend). 5 pruned with reason `fanout` (F-2-009 to F-2-013 under F-1-004\n160:   and F-1-006): the lineage node cap is 5 (half its 10-iteration budget), and 3 seeds + 2 growth\n161:   filled it at iteration 1. The pruned ones were good questions (for example F-2-012 \"measured setup\n162:   time per executor kind\"). The cap, not relevance, decided what the run studied.\n163: - The prune reason `fanout` names the run-wide node cap as well as the per-parent child cap\n164:   (`frontier-admit.cjs:774-781`), so the store cannot tell the operator which cap bit.\n165: - F-1-006 (cost and latency) closed `exhausted/budget` in the reducer's projection after one\n166:   pass: the depth-1 band (50% of 10 = 5 visits) was spent across the three seeds.\n167: \n168: ### P4. Node store and registry disagree on every node\n169: \n170: - After the run, `R/lineages/*/frontier-nodes.jsonl` shows every seed `open`, and no closes at all.\n171: - The reducer projection in each lineage's `findings-registry.json` says opus F-1-001, F-1-003 and\n172:   F-1-005 are `answered`, and deepseek's F-1-002, F-1-004, F-2-007 and F-2-008 `answered`, F-1-006\n173:   `exhausted/budget`.\n174: - In research the only close the workflow writes to the store is the stuck close\n175:   (`deep-research.yaml:1528`). Answered and budget states live only in the reducer's projection, so\n176:   the file named \"the node store\" is stale for every node that finished normally. The frontier veto\n177:   reads the projection (`convergence.cjs:1559`, `:1749`), so behavior is right; the store misleads.\n178: - This also explains why opus could stop `converged` at iteration 5 while its store shows three open\n179:   nodes: the projection had none open, so the `frontierOpen` veto (`convergence.cjs:1206-1218`)\n180:   correctly did not fire.\n181: \n182: ### P5. Deepseek left its partition after its frontier drained\n183: \n184: - Iterations 1-7 worked deepseek's own nodes. Iterations 8, 9 and 10 took their focus straight from\n185:   the topic: \"Q1 restraint\", \"Q5 design questions\", \"Q6 prior art\". Those are opus's F-1-001,\n186:   F-1-003 and F-1-005.\n187: - Cause: once the projection holds no open node, Next Focus falls back to the topic text, and the\n188:   topic names all six questions. The partition only bounds the frontier, not the topic.\n189: - `fanout-merge.cjs` reported `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`): the guard\n190:   checks node ids, so topic-driven work on another lineage's question is invisible to it.\n191: - Effect: Q1, Q5 and Q6 got a second, cheaper view. Useful for cross-checking, but it is unbudgeted\n192:   duplicate work. Deepseek's prior-art pass made 4 `webfetch` calls and cites 4 URLs (Anthropic's\n193:   multi-agent research post, LangChain open_deep_research, two arXiv papers); opus's cites 15.\n194: \n195: ### P6. Opus stopped converged after a blocked stop\n196: \n197: - Iteration 5 is a `blocked_stop` recovery: `source_diversity_guard`, `evidence_depth_guard` and\n198:   `uncovered_questions` blocked the stop although all three nodes were answered\n199:   (`R/lineages/opus/iterations/iteration-005.md`). Opus traced the cause itself: the graph guards\n200:   read only the optional `graphEvents` (`iteration-graph-upsert.cjs:122`), not the mandatory finding\n201:   rows. This costs one recovery iteration per lineage that follows the mandatory contract.\n202: - The `blocked_stop` row carries `stopReason: \"legacy-blocked-stop\"` and a whole-second stamp\n203:   (`01:34:29.000Z`), while opus's iteration rows carry milliseconds.\n204: - Deepseek recorded no `blocked_stop`, `stuckRecovery` or any convergence row: its ratio of 1 never\n205:   reached a stop candidate, so the guards never ran.\n206: \n207: ## Synthesis on the fan-out root\n208: \n209: ### Y1. `step_fanout_merge` worked\n210: \n211: - `fanout-merge.cjs --loop-type research` exit 0, 2 lineages, 192 key findings,\n212:   `frontier_partition_guard.passed: true` (`D/merge.out`). The partition guard missed P5's topic\n213:   drift, as noted.\n214: - `fanout-attribution.md` lists opus \"Convergence 0.55\" and deepseek \"1\": the last ratio, labeled\n215:   as convergence.\n216: \n217: ### Y2. `step_emit_resource_map` failed on the fan-out root: no root config\n218: \n219: - The `if_present` command exited 3 with `ENOENT ... research/deep-research-config.json`\n220:   (`D/resmap.err`), because `emitFanoutResourceMap` requires a root config\n221:   (`reduce-state.cjs:1816-1819`) and the fan-out path writes none.\n222: - The `:auto` setup is supposed to persist the config (`research.md:88`). But under `--restart`,\n223:   `step_apply_lifecycle_request` would then archive that fresh config with the old packet, and\n224:   `bind_prior_lineage` would read the new session as the \"prior\" one. **This is a contract\n225:   contradiction.** Across the corpus, 104 of 192 committed fan-out research roots have neither a root\n226:   config nor a resource map.\n227: - **Judgment call:** I wrote the root config late, from the skill's template\n228:   (`deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json`). It holds generation 3, the parent session\n229:   `2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z`, `lineageMode: restart` and the fan-out matrix. The rerun then\n230:   emitted `R/resource-map.md` from 15 delta files (`D/resmap2.out`).\n231: - Both lineages hit the lineage-side twin of this defect: the single-loop `if_absent` command\n232:   (`deep-research.yaml:2155`) carries no `{reducer_artifact_arg}`. Deepseek's map failed with\n233:   ENOENT; opus added `--artifact-dir` by hand.\n234: \n235: ### Y3. `step_compile_research`, closeout and config status\n236: \n237: - I wrote `R/research.md` from both lineage syntheses and iterations.\n238: - `step_convergence_report` ran as written. The closeout emitted\n239:   `deep_research.synthesis_complete` (`totalIterations: 15`) and the gateway appended it with a\n240:   receipt (`D/closeout.out`). The root row carries `lineageId` = the *prior* session\n241:   (`2026-11-17T10:36:36.000Z`), apparently taken from `parentSessionId`. That looks like a field\n242:   mix-up worth checking.\n243: - `step_update_config_status` set the late root config to `complete`.\n244: - The dashboard refresh and the terminal heartbeat skip on fan-out by design, so the root has **no\n245:   dashboard**, as in `PREV` P7.\n246: \n247: ### Y4. Deviations from the workflow (recorded)\n248: \n249: - I skipped `step_writeback_spec_findings` and its validation (they edit `SPEC/spec.md`), and\n250:   `phase_save --full-auto` (it writes continuity into packet docs). The brief is report-only with a\n251:   clean tree.\n252: - I restored the settle-time metadata refresh's rewrite of `SPEC/description.json` **and**\n253:   `SPEC/graph-metadata.json` (176-line diff in `D/metadata-refresh.diff`).\n254: \n255: ## Did the fixes since the review behave live?\n256: \n257: | Fix | Live result |\n258: |-----|-------------|\n259: | Fatal-failure stderr line (`f2de4f588c5`) | **Not exercised.** No lineage failed, so no terminal `failed` event fired. The code path is at `fanout-run.cjs:4185-4196`. |\n260: | Completion check (`a6c1332a331`, `1ea09919553`) | **Behaved, but it is weak for research.** Both lineages passed on `synthesis_complete`. Research's terminal set accepts any synthesis row, including `synthesis_incomplete` (`fanout-run.cjs:1248-1251`). Deepseek wrote no convergence or stop-gate row at all and still passed, the same gap `PREV` P6 named for review, which review closed with `terminal_gates`. |\n261: | Dry-run preview (`30c88ac2e2a`, `99a12d54838`, `377055592a5`) | **Worked.** It confirmed model, effort, sandbox, permission and config dir per lineage and wrote nothing. The topic text is not shown (digest only), so I confirmed it by rendering the prompt. Oddities are in S2. |\n262: | No `description.json` rewrite (`4c6a3a41f03`) | **Review only, by design.** The research fan-out still rewrote `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` at settle (`metadata_refresh_ok` x2 in `R/orchestration-status.log`), and the rewrite degraded both files. |\n263: | Log rotation on resume (`600d84b1677`) | **Not exercised.** There was no failed attempt and no resume. `fanout-lineage.out/.err` exist once per lineage, and no `.1` file exists. |\n264: | `--sandbox-mode` / `sandboxMode` for cli-claude-code | **Worked.** `bypassPermissions` in the preview and the live argv; opus ran Bash and recorded state. |\n265: | Per-lineage budget lines | **Worked**: `lineage opus budget 10 iterations, derived from its seed share`. |\n266: \n267: ## Lineage differences, side by side\n268: \n269: | Aspect | opus (cli-claude-code, claude-opus-5-5, medium) | deepseek (cli-opencode, llmgateway deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, max) |\n270: |---|---|---|\n271: | Wall clock | 20.1 min, 5 iterations | 13.7 min, 10 iterations |\n272: | Per iteration | 2 to 5 min | 0.5 to 1.6 min |\n273: | Stop | converged after 1 blocked stop (graph guards) | maxIterationsReached; no stop machinery ran |\n274: | Ratio | 0.93, 0.88, 0.75, 0.83, 0.55 | 1.0 on all 10 |\n275: | Growth proposals | 0 | 7 (2 admitted, 5 pruned by the node cap) |\n276: | Partition discipline | stayed on its 3 nodes | drifted into opus's Q1, Q5 and Q6 at iterations 8-10 |\n277: | Citations per pass | 46 in iteration 1 | 11 to 22 |\n278: | Web | 15 URLs | 4 URLs (4 `webfetch` calls) |\n279: | Resource map | worked around the missing `--artifact-dir` | failed with ENOENT and reported it |\n280: | Cost data | none (text output) | $0.326, 164 steps |\n281: | Workflow hygiene | self-reported one `sed -i` and one shell-redirect write against the prompt pack's rules | no self-report |\n282: \n283: ## Top frictions\n284: \n285: 1. The fan-out root has no config, so the resource map fails, the config status cannot be set and the\n286:    restart lineage chain is lost (Y2, S4).\n287: 2. The resource-map step drops the lineage artifact dir; both lineages hit it (Y2).\n288: 3. Expansive partitioning leaks: a drained lineage works other lineages' questions from the topic\n289:    (P5).\n290: 4. The node cap prunes growth at iteration 1, and the derived budget is a constant 10 for any\n291:    2-lineage research run (P3, S3).\n292: 5. The research completion check accepts a lineage that ran no stop machinery (fix table).\n293: 6. The node store says every node is open after a converged run (P4).\n294: 7. The research fan-out still rewrites and degrades packet metadata outside `research/` (Y4).\n295: 8. No root dashboard, and no per-lineage status in the summary (Y3).\n296: \n297: ## Commit\n298: \n299: - Commit `adade6c293e` (amended from `b37964ab6d5` to correct backlog rows 2 and 9) on `worktrees/455-expansive-depth-integration` (subject 71 characters, no\n300:   attribution lines). It holds 244 files: `research/` (root, both lineages, raw logs, the backlog)\n301:   and `research_archive/20261120T011847Z/` (69 renames plus files git did not pair).\n302: - The YAML's `step_stage_artifact_dir` command exited 1, because its exclude pathspec names the\n303:   gitignored `.legacy-projection-watermarks` and git refuses an ignored path even in an exclude.\n304:   Everything else staged; the step's `on_fail` is a warning.\n305: - The repo's pre-commit gate `[gate:spec-remint]` re-derived `SPEC/graph-metadata.json` and staged it\n306:   into the commit (`D/commit.out`). It correctly drops the archived root `research/` paths, but it\n307:   also drops the trigger phrases `depth-mode expansive` and `frontier veto`, the same loss as the\n308:   runner's settle-time refresh. `description.json` was not touched. I did not fight the hook.\n309: - The hook asked for no dsh mirror sync. The tree was clean after the commit. All captured PIDs\n310:   (39805, 39806, 39812, 44925 and 44931) had exited by themselves; none was killed, and the 180-minute\n311:   watchdog never fired."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/scratch/dogfood-research-gen3.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795179519941,"end":1795179520038}}}}
