{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179686998,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f90c2a0d001rDN8GE171X5jvN","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f90c0fcb001HKXBAnzCjV39vF","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-858f18bdcc4a54d8","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"outcome\\|session\\|resume\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts | sed -n '1,10p'; echo \"--- dsh home ---\"; grep -n \"createDshHome\\|dshHome\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs | head -20"},"output":"25:// A guard refusal is a route violation, not an executor outcome. It must not read as\n82:// Pi's session environment variable is unconfirmed; leave this kind absent\n83:// until the live contract identifies a real session identifier.\n84:// Vibe's session env is unconfirmed too; the kind stays absent rather than carrying a guessed name.\n90:  // its own subprocess env, matching the --output-format json `session_id` field.\n126:// has no useful answer left: refusing on it leaves a Pi session with no way to hand work out\n144:  // Spec-gate + child-session control for dispatched CLI workers. Without these,\n148:  // as an orchestrated child session rather than a new top-level session.\n162:  // share this prefix. No session-id env var is documented or observed, so\n241:  // The run's session id. On a ledger-backed state log it scopes the failure\n--- dsh home ---\n3215:let dshHomeSweepRegistered = false;\n3268:function createDshHome() {\n3272:  if (!dshHomeSweepRegistered) {\n3273:    dshHomeSweepRegistered = true;\n4262:      const dshHome = lineage.kind === 'cli-deepseek-harness'\n4263:        ? createDshHome()\n4319:        ...(dshHome ? { DSH_HOME: dshHome } : {}),\n4669:      if (dshHome) removeDshHome(dshHome);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"25:// A guard refusal is a route violation, not an executor outcome. It must not read as\n82:// Pi's session environment variable is unconfirmed; leave this kind absent\n83:// until the live contract identifies a real session identifier.\n84:// Vibe's session env is unconfirmed too; the kind stays absent rather than carrying a guessed name.\n90:  // its own subprocess env, matching the --output-format json `session_id` field.\n126:// has no useful answer left: refusing on it leaves a Pi session with no way to hand work out\n144:  // Spec-gate + child-session control for dispatched CLI workers. Without these,\n148:  // as an orchestrated child session rather than a new top-level session.\n162:  // share this prefix. No session-id env var is documented or observed, so\n241:  // The run's session id. On a ledger-backed state log it scopes the failure\n--- dsh home ---\n3215:let dshHomeSweepRegistered = false;\n3268:function createDshHome() {\n3272:  if (!dshHomeSweepRegistered) {\n3273:    dshHomeSweepRegistered = true;\n4262:      const dshHome = lineage.kind === 'cli-deepseek-harness'\n4263:        ? createDshHome()\n4319:        ...(dshHome ? { DSH_HOME: dshHome } : {}),\n4669:      if (dshHome) removeDshHome(dshHome);\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"outcome\\\\|session\\\\|resume\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts | sed -n '1,10p'; echo \\\"--- dsh home ---\\\"; grep -n \\\"createDshHome\\\\|dshHome\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1795179686413,"end":1795179686998}}}}
