{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795179776912,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f90d8a19001A717c1dQbM9zHE","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f90d821c001pzbHLxkcH1nJrv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6d6a68b16c0f86c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"no finding attached\\|answeredQuestions\\|answersQuestion\\|finding\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs | head -40"},"output":"169:// A review leaf names a finding node with its own prefix and case around the finding\n170:// id. The graph keeps one finding node per finding, so `finding-R1-P1-001`,\n171:// `finding-r1-p1-001`, `FIND-R1-P1-001`, `node:finding:R1-P1-001` and the bare id all\n172:// fold onto the node the finding is stored under. `knownFindings` maps each lowercased\n173:// finding id of this iteration and of the stored graph to that node id. The raw id is\n174:// tried before its prefix is stripped, so an id that itself starts with `finding-`\n176:const FINDING_ID_PREFIX = /^(?:node:)?(?:finding|find)[:_-](.+)$/i;\n178:// The node a known finding is stored under, or null when the id names no known\n179:// finding. An edge endpoint folds only onto a finding that exists.\n194:  return match ? `finding:${match[1]}` : null;\n197:// A file:line ref names a place a finding can be checked; a bare path does not. The\n224:      // A torn line carries no finding; the reducer reports corruption separately.\n230:// The iteration's own findings are the source of review evidence: each finding with\n232:// of that path. The evidence-density signal counts those edges per finding, and a\n234:// could never allow a stop. The delta's finding rows carry the ref the leaf\n235:// contract requires; the state record's findingDetails may leave it out.\n238:  const add = (finding) => {\n239:    if (!finding || typeof finding.id !== 'string' || !finding.id.trim()) return;\n240:    const id = finding.id.trim();\n242:    const file = typeof finding.file === 'string' && finding.file.trim() ? finding.file.trim() : null;\n243:    if (!known) byId.set(id, { id, title: finding.title, file });\n249:      if (row && row.type === 'finding' && (row.iteration === undefined || Number(row.iteration) === iteration)) add(row);\n257:    for (const finding of record && Array.isArray(record.findingDetails) ? record.findingDetails : []) add(finding);\n263:// different finding (another file and another title) gets a node keyed on the id and\n264:// this iteration, the way the reducer keeps two such findings apart.\n265:function deriveReviewFindingEvidence(findings, iteration, storedNode = () => null) {\n268:  for (const finding of findings) {\n269:    if (!finding || typeof finding.id !== 'string' || !finding.id.trim()) continue;\n270:    const rawId = finding.id.trim();\n271:    const ref = parseFindingRef(finding.file);\n272:    const title = typeof finding.title === 'string' && finding.title ? finding.title : rawId;\n273:    const stored = storedNode(`finding:${rawId}`);\n280:    const findingId = distinct ? `finding:${rawId}#${iteration}` : `finding:${rawId}`;\n282:      id: findingId,\n286:      metadata: { finding_id: rawId, ...(ref ? { file: ref.filePath, line: ref.line } : {}) },\n292:      id: `evidence:${findingId.slice('finding:'.length)}:${fileId}`,\n294:      sourceId: findingId,\n296:      metadata: { derivedFrom: 'findingDetails', line: ref.line },\n303:// from a value the leaf sends, so source diversity rises only when a finding cites\n354:// A research iteration's finding rows and the question texts it answered. The\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"169:// A review leaf names a finding node with its own prefix and case around the finding\n170:// id. The graph keeps one finding node per finding, so `finding-R1-P1-001`,\n171:// `finding-r1-p1-001`, `FIND-R1-P1-001`, `node:finding:R1-P1-001` and the bare id all\n172:// fold onto the node the finding is stored under. `knownFindings` maps each lowercased\n173:// finding id of this iteration and of the stored graph to that node id. The raw id is\n174:// tried before its prefix is stripped, so an id that itself starts with `finding-`\n176:const FINDING_ID_PREFIX = /^(?:node:)?(?:finding|find)[:_-](.+)$/i;\n178:// The node a known finding is stored under, or null when the id names no known\n179:// finding. An edge endpoint folds only onto a finding that exists.\n194:  return match ? `finding:${match[1]}` : null;\n197:// A file:line ref names a place a finding can be checked; a bare path does not. The\n224:      // A torn line carries no finding; the reducer reports corruption separately.\n230:// The iteration's own findings are the source of review evidence: each finding with\n232:// of that path. The evidence-density signal counts those edges per finding, and a\n234:// could never allow a stop. The delta's finding rows carry the ref the leaf\n235:// contract requires; the state record's findingDetails may leave it out.\n238:  const add = (finding) => {\n239:    if (!finding || typeof finding.id !== 'string' || !finding.id.trim()) return;\n240:    const id = finding.id.trim();\n242:    const file = typeof finding.file === 'string' && finding.file.trim() ? finding.file.trim() : null;\n243:    if (!known) byId.set(id, { id, title: finding.title, file });\n249:      if (row && row.type === 'finding' && (row.iteration === undefined || Number(row.iteration) === iteration)) add(row);\n257:    for (const finding of record && Array.isArray(record.findingDetails) ? record.findingDetails : []) add(finding);\n263:// different finding (another file and another title) gets a node keyed on the id and\n264:// this iteration, the way the reducer keeps two such findings apart.\n265:function deriveReviewFindingEvidence(findings, iteration, storedNode = () => null) {\n268:  for (const finding of findings) {\n269:    if (!finding || typeof finding.id !== 'string' || !finding.id.trim()) continue;\n270:    const rawId = finding.id.trim();\n271:    const ref = parseFindingRef(finding.file);\n272:    const title = typeof finding.title === 'string' && finding.title ? finding.title : rawId;\n273:    const stored = storedNode(`finding:${rawId}`);\n280:    const findingId = distinct ? `finding:${rawId}#${iteration}` : `finding:${rawId}`;\n282:      id: findingId,\n286:      metadata: { finding_id: rawId, ...(ref ? { file: ref.filePath, line: ref.line } : {}) },\n292:      id: `evidence:${findingId.slice('finding:'.length)}:${fileId}`,\n294:      sourceId: findingId,\n296:      metadata: { derivedFrom: 'findingDetails', line: ref.line },\n303:// from a value the leaf sends, so source diversity rises only when a finding cites\n354:// A research iteration's finding rows and the question texts it answered. The\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"no finding attached\\\\|answeredQuestions\\\\|answersQuestion\\\\|finding\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1795179776537,"end":1795179776912}}}}
