{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795180021386,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f9113196001D2ZXgRR46Ci632","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9112a8b001iCLpPBBaKxrZv3","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acf5cc0b6ad804e6","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 4: F-1-002 adapter contract and conformance test (synthesis)\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope fanout-run.cjs LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts, runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .claude .codex .pi .dsh .vibe .opencode mirrors against .skilled): Cross-LI execution contract: where do permission and sandbox, effort, output format, session resume, failure classes, log shape and prompt channel still differ across LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, executor-config.ts and dispatch-iteration.cjs, and what single adapter contract and conformance test (agent and command mirrors included) would remove the differences?\n\nThis pass is analytical: iteration 1 gathered the differences, so the remaining work is the contract shape and the test that would hold it. No new external source is introduced, which is why the status is `insight` rather than `complete`.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Re-read iteration 1's findings and the builders they cite, plus `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` and `effective_config`.\n2. Checked that `buildLineageCommand` is the shared entrypoint the single-executor cursor/devin/pi branch already calls, so a table-driven test can target one function rather than eight.\n3. Checked the stress matrix's fourteen rows and the `expectSuccessArgs` switch that duplicates the builders.\n4. Composed the contract fields so each one maps to a difference that iteration 1 confirmed, and wrote the four fixture assertions.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The contract is one record per `ExecutorKind` with seven capability fields, and every field answers a difference this run found.** The fields are `binary`, `promptChannel` (`argv`/`stdin`/`file`), `outputFormat` (`text`/`json`/`export`/`none`), `costSource` (`step_finish`/`export`/null), `effortSurface` (`flag`/`model-suffix`/`model-id`/`config`/`none`), `sandboxSurface` (`os-flag`/`approval-flag`/`tool-allowlist`/`none`) and `resume` (`session-flag`/`artifact-only`/`none`). It belongs beside `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, which already declares what each kind accepts but not how it is carried. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:32]\n\n2. **The conformance test is four fixture assertions over `buildLineageCommand`, one per divergence that is currently undetected.** (a) Given a fixed lineage and a prompt, exactly one channel carries it: one `promptArgIndexes` entry, or `input === prompt` with a trailing `-`, or a `--prompt-file` path; `redactedArgs` must show one digest. (b) A requested `--sandbox-mode` round-trips into `effectiveConfig.sandboxEnforcement`, or the adapter refuses it; today five single-executor branches silently substitute `workspace-write`. (c) A synthetic log fixture per `costSource` must make `sumProviderCostFromLog` return the declared shape or null, so a null is labelled rather than anonymous. (d) A synthetic transcript per pending-question source must yield the expected `detectPendingQuestion` result, which today can never be true for a JSON log. [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:42] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76]\n\n3. **The test should iterate `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and fail on an unlisted kind, which retires the `expectSuccessArgs` switch instead of extending it.** The stress suite's per-kind switch is a second copy of each builder's decisions; a table-driven test reads the same contract the builder reads, so a new kind cannot be added with a builder and no assertions, or with assertions and no builder. The fourteen existing edge-case rows stay as they are; four adapter-contract rows are added to the matrix so the bijection validator covers them. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:92] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:18]\n\n4. **The build order is: contract table and test first (S), then the held rows in F-1-004's order (30+12, then 13, then 29).** The contract is the cheap artifact that makes row 13's collapse safe: row 13 removes the hand-built `runClaude`/`runCodex` branches, and without the four assertions the collapse can re-introduce the sandbox substitution or the text-format cost gap silently. The mirror half needs no work: both gates pass, and the missing command trees in `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` are the crosswalk's sanctioned shape. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:961] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:53] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:67]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Where do the eight kinds still differ? Iteration 1, Findings 1-5.\n- What single adapter contract and conformance test would remove the differences, including the mirrors? Findings 1-4: a seven-field capability record and four fixture assertions over `buildLineageCommand`, with no new mirror gate.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- None for this node. The contract shape is decided; implementation, value/effort/risk and the row-13 sequencing are recorded in the ledger for F-1-004's order.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nFrontier node F-2-007: whether the cli-adapter stress suite is part of a default gate and which matrix cells remain pending.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Deriving the contract from the CLI help text at test time.** The adapters are pinned to live-verified flags, and a help probe cannot prove the runner reads the log shape the flag produces.\n- **One test per adapter kind written by hand.** That is the current `expectSuccessArgs` shape; it duplicates the builder and drifts with it.\n- **Treating the contract as documentation only.** The point is that the builder and the test read one table; a prose table with no consumer is another document to rot.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a capability record already shipped under another name: `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` is the closest, and it answers \"is the field accepted\", not \"how is it carried\".\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none. The node's two questions were answered in iteration 1 and this pass.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: this is a synthesis pass; newInfoRatio is reported as `insight` because no new external evidence was gathered.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:961`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:18`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:92`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:32`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:53`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.60\n- Questions addressed: the adapter contract shape and the conformance test.\n- Questions answered: the F-1-002 question in full.\n- Finding mix: four partially new synthesis findings, plus the +0.10 simplicity bonus for collapsing six builder-level differences into one seven-field record and four assertions.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: mapping every contract field to a difference found in iteration 1 kept the design from becoming an aspiration; each field has a failure it prevents and a file:line that shows the failure today.\n- What did not work and why: I considered a per-kind test list first, which would have recreated the duplication the test exists to remove; the table-driven shape only emerged after reading `expectSuccessArgs`.\n- What I would do differently: write the four assertions in the same pass as the contract, because an assertion that cannot be written is a field that does not describe observable behaviour.\n\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 4: F-1-002 adapter contract and conformance test (synthesis)\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope fanout-run.cjs LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts, runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .claude .codex .pi .dsh .vibe .opencode mirrors against .skilled): Cross-LI execution contract: where do permission and sandbox, effort, output format, session resume, failure classes, log shape and prompt channel still differ across LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, executor-config.ts and dispatch-iteration.cjs, and what single adapter contract and conformance test (agent and command mirrors included) would remove the differences?\\n\\nThis pass is analytical: iteration 1 gathered the differences, so the remaining work is the contract shape and the test that would hold it. No new external source is introduced, which is why the status is `insight` rather than `complete`.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Re-read iteration 1's findings and the builders they cite, plus `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` and `effective_config`.\\n2. Checked that `buildLineageCommand` is the shared entrypoint the single-executor cursor/devin/pi branch already calls, so a table-driven test can target one function rather than eight.\\n3. Checked the stress matrix's fourteen rows and the `expectSuccessArgs` switch that duplicates the builders.\\n4. Composed the contract fields so each one maps to a difference that iteration 1 confirmed, and wrote the four fixture assertions.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The contract is one record per `ExecutorKind` with seven capability fields, and every field answers a difference this run found.** The fields are `binary`, `promptChannel` (`argv`/`stdin`/`file`), `outputFormat` (`text`/`json`/`export`/`none`), `costSource` (`step_finish`/`export`/null), `effortSurface` (`flag`/`model-suffix`/`model-id`/`config`/`none`), `sandboxSurface` (`os-flag`/`approval-flag`/`tool-allowlist`/`none`) and `resume` (`session-flag`/`artifact-only`/`none`). It belongs beside `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, which already declares what each kind accepts but not how it is carried. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:32]\\n\\n2. **The conformance test is four fixture assertions over `buildLineageCommand`, one per divergence that is currently undetected.** (a) Given a fixed lineage and a prompt, exactly one channel carries it: one `promptArgIndexes` entry, or `input === prompt` with a trailing `-`, or a `--prompt-file` path; `redactedArgs` must show one digest. (b) A requested `--sandbox-mode` round-trips into `effectiveConfig.sandboxEnforcement`, or the adapter refuses it; today five single-executor branches silently substitute `workspace-write`. (c) A synthetic log fixture per `costSource` must make `sumProviderCostFromLog` return the declared shape or null, so a null is labelled rather than anonymous. (d) A synthetic transcript per pending-question source must yield the expected `detectPendingQuestion` result, which today can never be true for a JSON log. [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:42] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76]\\n\\n3. **The test should iterate `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and fail on an unlisted kind, which retires the `expectSuccessArgs` switch instead of extending it.** The stress suite's per-kind switch is a second copy of each builder's decisions; a table-driven test reads the same contract the builder reads, so a new kind cannot be added with a builder and no assertions, or with assertions and no builder. The fourteen existing edge-case rows stay as they are; four adapter-contract rows are added to the matrix so the bijection validator covers them. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:92] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:18]\\n\\n4. **The build order is: contract table and test first (S), then the held rows in F-1-004's order (30+12, then 13, then 29).** The contract is the cheap artifact that makes row 13's collapse safe: row 13 removes the hand-built `runClaude`/`runCodex` branches, and without the four assertions the collapse can re-introduce the sandbox substitution or the text-format cost gap silently. The mirror half needs no work: both gates pass, and the missing command trees in `.codex`, `.pi`, `.dsh` and `.vibe` are the crosswalk's sanctioned shape. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:961] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:53] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:67]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Where do the eight kinds still differ? Iteration 1, Findings 1-5.\\n- What single adapter contract and conformance test would remove the differences, including the mirrors? Findings 1-4: a seven-field capability record and four fixture assertions over `buildLineageCommand`, with no new mirror gate.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- None for this node. The contract shape is decided; implementation, value/effort/risk and the row-13 sequencing are recorded in the ledger for F-1-004's order.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-2-007: whether the cli-adapter stress suite is part of a default gate and which matrix cells remain pending.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Deriving the contract from the CLI help text at test time.** The adapters are pinned to live-verified flags, and a help probe cannot prove the runner reads the log shape the flag produces.\\n- **One test per adapter kind written by hand.** That is the current `expectSuccessArgs` shape; it duplicates the builder and drifts with it.\\n- **Treating the contract as documentation only.** The point is that the builder and the test read one table; a prose table with no consumer is another document to rot.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a capability record already shipped under another name: `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` is the closest, and it answers \\\"is the field accepted\\\", not \\\"how is it carried\\\".\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none. The node's two questions were answered in iteration 1 and this pass.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: this is a synthesis pass; newInfoRatio is reported as `insight` because no new external evidence was gathered.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:112`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:961`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:18`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fixtures/adapter-suite.ts:92`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:32`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md:53`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.60\\n- Questions addressed: the adapter contract shape and the conformance test.\\n- Questions answered: the F-1-002 question in full.\\n- Finding mix: four partially new synthesis findings, plus the +0.10 simplicity bonus for collapsing six builder-level differences into one seven-field record and four assertions.\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: mapping every contract field to a difference found in iteration 1 kept the design from becoming an aspiration; each field has a failure it prevents and a file:line that shows the failure today.\\n- What did not work and why: I considered a per-kind test list first, which would have recreated the duplication the test exists to remove; the table-driven shape only emerged after reading `expectSuccessArgs`.\\n- What I would do differently: write the four assertions in the same pass as the contract, because an assertion that cannot be written is a field that does not describe observable behaviour.\\n\\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\\n\\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795180016022,"end":1795180021386}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1795180022924,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f9114c8c001yfMrEERpcWqrXZ","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9112a8b001iCLpPBBaKxrZv3","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"574cc88836317fafdddc80bcceba9ade69b4676e","cost":0.003017496,"tokens":{"input":1179,"output":2296,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":236224,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795180025031,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f91154c7001OQSFmTIYTQtxM5","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9114c930012LhhyL3lt23Aax","type":"step-start","snapshot":"574cc88836317fafdddc80bcceba9ade69b4676e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795180025557,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f9115537001ocJgDVRS4hR1TY","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f9114c930012LhhyL3lt23Aax","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ed3a4b63463b0ce","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"^\\*\\*\\|^1\\. \\*\\*\\|^2\\. \\*\\*\\|^3\\. \\*\\*\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md | head -12; echo \"--- iter2 line of finding 5 ---\"; grep -n \"^\\*\\*The four held rows\\|^5\\. \\*\\*The four held\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"19:1. **`--sandbox-mode` round-trips for only three of the eight kinds; five single-executor branches hardcode `workspace-write`.** `runClaude` derives the Claude permission mode from `context.sandboxMode` and `runResearchOpencode` resolves `context.sandboxMode` (falling back to `danger-full-access`), but `runCodex` sets `sandboxMode: 'workspace-write'`, `runLineageBuiltin` (cursor, devin, pi) sets `const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write'`, and `runDeepseekHarness` sets it the same way. A documented `--sandbox-mode=read-only` therefore becomes `workspace-write` on five kinds with no warning, and the audit row records the hardcoded value, not the requested one. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:421] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:483] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:902]\n21:2. **The iteration prompt travels over three channels and no adapter declares which one it uses.** `promptArgIndexes: [1]` for claude and cursor, `[args.length - 1]` for opencode and pi, `input: prompt` with an empty argv for codex and dsh, and `--prompt-file` with no argv prompt for vibe. The redaction and fingerprint code handles all three, but neither `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` nor `effective_config` publishes `promptChannel`, and nothing enforces a maximum prompt size on the argv channel (the dogfood prompts were 46k characters). A single contract field would let a dispatch refuse or switch channel before spawn. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2684] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2721] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2792] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3192] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3368] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3587]\n23:3. **Cost observability is one adapter's log shape, and the summary publishes a null without saying which kinds are unknown.** `sumProviderCostFromLog` sums only `{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"part\":{\"cost\":…}}` rows, which is opencode's shape. Claude and Cursor request `--output-format text`, Codex, Pi and Devin pass no format flag, and Vibe writes a separate export, so `provider_cost_usd.by_lineage` is null for those kinds and `total` is null for the run. That honest roll-up has no per-kind capability statement, so an operator cannot tell \"unknown cost\" from \"kind cannot report cost\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2713] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2970] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4969]\n--- iter2 line of finding 5 ---\n27:5. **The four held rows have a dependency order: 30 + 12 as one change, then 13 with the adapter capability test, then 29 last.** Row 12 (one `projectFrontier`) is the shared parser and projection; row 30 (per-node research dashboard) is the renderer that consumes it, and the backlog already pairs them. Row 13 (one executor path) is independent of the frontier work but needs row 2's permission fix (delivered) and the capability manifest from F-1-002 to keep the merged path honest; doing it before 29 also removes the hand-built branches that make some aliases look live. Row 29 deletes config-key aliases, legacy migration and binary probes; it is safest after 12 and 13, because those two changes decide which keys and probes have no caller. Building 29 first would delete aliases whose only remaining reader is a branch that 13 has not yet collapsed. [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:43] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:44] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:60] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:61]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"19:1. **`--sandbox-mode` round-trips for only three of the eight kinds; five single-executor branches hardcode `workspace-write`.** `runClaude` derives the Claude permission mode from `context.sandboxMode` and `runResearchOpencode` resolves `context.sandboxMode` (falling back to `danger-full-access`), but `runCodex` sets `sandboxMode: 'workspace-write'`, `runLineageBuiltin` (cursor, devin, pi) sets `const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write'`, and `runDeepseekHarness` sets it the same way. A documented `--sandbox-mode=read-only` therefore becomes `workspace-write` on five kinds with no warning, and the audit row records the hardcoded value, not the requested one. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:421] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:483] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:538] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs:902]\n21:2. **The iteration prompt travels over three channels and no adapter declares which one it uses.** `promptArgIndexes: [1]` for claude and cursor, `[args.length - 1]` for opencode and pi, `input: prompt` with an empty argv for codex and dsh, and `--prompt-file` with no argv prompt for vibe. The redaction and fingerprint code handles all three, but neither `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT` nor `effective_config` publishes `promptChannel`, and nothing enforces a maximum prompt size on the argv channel (the dogfood prompts were 46k characters). A single contract field would let a dispatch refuse or switch channel before spawn. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2684] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2721] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2792] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3192] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3368] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3587]\n23:3. **Cost observability is one adapter's log shape, and the summary publishes a null without saying which kinds are unknown.** `sumProviderCostFromLog` sums only `{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"part\":{\"cost\":…}}` rows, which is opencode's shape. Claude and Cursor request `--output-format text`, Codex, Pi and Devin pass no format flag, and Vibe writes a separate export, so `provider_cost_usd.by_lineage` is null for those kinds and `total` is null for the run. That honest roll-up has no per-kind capability statement, so an operator cannot tell \"unknown cost\" from \"kind cannot report cost\". [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-salvage.cjs:76] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2713] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2970] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4969]\n--- iter2 line of finding 5 ---\n27:5. **The four held rows have a dependency order: 30 + 12 as one change, then 13 with the adapter capability test, then 29 last.** Row 12 (one `projectFrontier`) is the shared parser and projection; row 30 (per-node research dashboard) is the renderer that consumes it, and the backlog already pairs them. Row 13 (one executor path) is independent of the frontier work but needs row 2's permission fix (delivered) and the capability manifest from F-1-002 to keep the merged path honest; doing it before 29 also removes the hand-built branches that make some aliases look live. Row 29 deletes config-key aliases, legacy migration and binary probes; it is safest after 12 and 13, because those two changes decide which keys and probes have no caller. Building 29 first would delete aliases whose only remaining reader is a branch that 13 has not yet collapsed. [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:43] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:44] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:60] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research_archive/20261120T125555Z/improvement-backlog.md:61]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"^\\\\*\\\\*\\\\|^1\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*\\\\|^2\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*\\\\|^3\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md | head -12; echo \\\"--- iter2 line of finding 5 ---\\\"; grep -n \\\"^\\\\*\\\\*The four held rows\\\\|^5\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*The four held\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795180025143,"end":1795180025557}}}}
