ormance test (synthesis)\n \n ## Focus\n \n-Frontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope fanout-run.cjs LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts, runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .claude .codex .pi .dsh .vibe .opencode mirrors against .skilled): Cross-LI execution contract: where do permission and sandbox, effort, output format, session resume, failure classes, log shape and prompt channel still differ across LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, executor-config.ts and dispatch-iteration.cjs, and what single adapter contract and conformance test (agent and command mirrors included) would remove the differences?\n+Frontier node F-1-002 (depth 1, scope fanout-run.cjs LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts, runtime/scripts/dispatch-iteration.cjs, .claude .codex .pi .dsh .vibe .opencode mirrors against .skilled): Cross-CLI execution contract: where do permission and sandbox, effort, output format, session resume, failure classes, log shape and prompt channel still differ across LINEAGE_COMMAND_ADAPTERS, executor-config.ts and dispatch-iteration.cjs, and what single adapter contract and conformance test (agent and command mirrors included) would remove the differences?\n \n This pass is analytical: iteration 1 gathered the differences, so the remaining work is the contract shape and the test that would hold it. No new external source is introduced, which is why the status is `insight` rather than `complete`.\n \n ## Actions Taken\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004