{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795180117705,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f912bec9001PT1r3MknBwHkuf","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f912b55b001t5ypwDSKBH0adD","type":"step-start","snapshot":"bd7a24970ee02b8728684970e2bc6fe00bbee374"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795180124329,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f912bece0017Vt1DlHzmXs4H3","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f912b55b001t5ypwDSKBH0adD","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af6485c59d949783","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: F-2-007 stress-suite gating and pending cells\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-2-007 (depth 2, scope runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter, package.json, CI workflow files): Is the cli-adapter stress suite part of any default test or CI gate, and which matrix cells remain pending at HEAD?\n\nThe node was read as: prove the gate wiring from the config and workflow, then run the matrix's own bijection validator so \"pending\" is a measured state rather than a table reading.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the runtime `package.json` and `vitest.config.ts` project definitions.\n2. Read `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml`, including its path filters and the `npm test` step.\n3. Read `matrix-manifest.ts`'s raw matrix, phase-two overlay and audit object.\n4. Ran `validate-playbook-package.cjs`, then ran the underlying `vitest list` command to find why it reported zero discovered tests.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The stress suite is in the default test run and in CI, so the adapter contracts are gated.** `vitest.config.ts` puts `tests/stress/**/*.{vitest,test}.ts` in the serial project, which `npm test` (`vitest run --no-coverage`) collects. `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml` runs that same command on pull requests and pushes touching `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/**` or `.skilled/commands/deep/**`. A change to an adapter or to the matrix therefore runs the hermetic adapter suites. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/package.json:1] [SOURCE: .github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:74]\n\n2. **Zero cells are pending in the matrix the audit reads.** `CLI_ADAPTER_STRESS_MATRIX` is the seed table with `testStatus: pending` for every non-codex cell, but `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX` overlays `CLI_ADAPTER_PHASE_TWO_ROWS` and `CLI_ADAPTER_FANOUT_ROWS` on it, and the audit tests that overlay. `fanout.vitest.ts` asserts `allAdapterBound: true`, `allSubjectBound: true` and no forbidden overclaims, and that assertion is part of the gated suite. Reading the seed table alone would wrongly report 112 pending cells. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:132] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:147] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fanout.vitest.ts:359]\n\n3. **The matrix's bijection validator fails at HEAD with 126 of 126 tests \"missing\", because its parser cannot read the current `vitest list` output.** The validator spawns `npx --no-install vitest list tests/stress/cli-adapter --configLoader runner` and keeps only lines that start with `tests/stress/cli-adapter`, but the current output prefixes every line with the project name, for example `[serial] tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-pi.vitest.ts > ...`. It discovers 0 tests and reports 126 missing, exit 1. The test bodies and the phase-two names exist; the parser is stale. Stripping an optional `[...] ` prefix would restore the bijection. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:100] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:116]\n\n4. **No workflow runs that validator, so its FAIL is invisible.** A search of `.github/workflows` finds the sk-doc `validate-playbook-package.cjs` in `playbook-operator-contract.yml`, but no invocation of the cli-adapter validator; the deep-loop workflow runs only the vitest suite. The manifest-integrity test checks the audit object, not the test-name bijection, so the two halves of the claim are separately gated and one half is not gated at all. [SOURCE: .github/workflows/playbook-operator-contract.yml:67] [SOURCE: .github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:86]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Is the cli-adapter stress suite part of a default test or CI gate? Yes: default `npm test` via the serial project, and the deep-loop CI workflow on the relevant paths. Finding 1.\n- Which matrix cells remain pending at HEAD? None in `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX`; the seed table's pending cells are overlaid by implemented phase-two and fanout rows. Finding 2.\n- Why does the matrix validator disagree? Finding 3: a stale parser, not missing tests. Finding 4: the validator is not wired into CI.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Whether the validator should be a vitest test in the gated suite or a workflow step; the test placement is cheaper to keep honest.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nFrontier node F-2-008: whether any runner path reads `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and persists a provider session id for a `--only-lineage` rerun.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Treating `CLI_ADAPTER_STRESS_MATRIX` as the live matrix.** The overlay is the live object and the audit proves it; the seed table is documentation of the phase-one state.\n- **Adding another CI workflow for the validator.** The existing deep-loop workflow already installs and runs the suite; one added step is enough.\n- **Rewriting the validator to import the tests instead of listing them.** `vitest list` is the supported discovery surface; the parser, not the mechanism, is wrong.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Grepping workflows for `cli-adapter` or `validate-playbook-package`: only the sk-doc validator appears, which is a different path and a different package.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"pending at HEAD\" could mean the seed table or the audit view. Both are reported; the audit view is the one that gates.\n- Contradictory evidence: the README says the validator \"proves that each row resolves to exactly one running test\"; the run shows 126 missing. The README describes the intent, the parser is stale. Recorded, not collapsed.\n- Missing dependencies: none. `npx --no-install vitest` resolved locally.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/package.json:1`\n- `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:74`\n- `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:86`\n- `.github/workflows/playbook-operator-contract.yml:67`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:132`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:147`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fanout.vitest.ts:359`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:100`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:116`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.75\n- Questions addressed: gate wiring and pending-cell state.\n- Questions answered: both.\n- Finding mix: 2 fully new (the stale parser, the unwired validator) and 2 partially new confirmations (the serial-project gate, the overlay).\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: running the validator and then its underlying command separated \"the tests are missing\" from \"the parser is stale\" in two calls; the exit code alone would have been misleading.\n- What did not work and why: reading the seed matrix first suggested 112 pending cells; only the overlay and the audit made the live state clear.\n- What I would do differently: start from `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX` and the audit, then explain the seed table as history, rather than the reverse.\n\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: F-2-007 stress-suite gating and pending cells\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-2-007 (depth 2, scope runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter, package.json, CI workflow files): Is the cli-adapter stress suite part of any default test or CI gate, and which matrix cells remain pending at HEAD?\\n\\nThe node was read as: prove the gate wiring from the config and workflow, then run the matrix's own bijection validator so \\\"pending\\\" is a measured state rather than a table reading.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the runtime `package.json` and `vitest.config.ts` project definitions.\\n2. Read `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml`, including its path filters and the `npm test` step.\\n3. Read `matrix-manifest.ts`'s raw matrix, phase-two overlay and audit object.\\n4. Ran `validate-playbook-package.cjs`, then ran the underlying `vitest list` command to find why it reported zero discovered tests.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **The stress suite is in the default test run and in CI, so the adapter contracts are gated.** `vitest.config.ts` puts `tests/stress/**/*.{vitest,test}.ts` in the serial project, which `npm test` (`vitest run --no-coverage`) collects. `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml` runs that same command on pull requests and pushes touching `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/**` or `.skilled/commands/deep/**`. A change to an adapter or to the matrix therefore runs the hermetic adapter suites. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/package.json:1] [SOURCE: .github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:74]\\n\\n2. **Zero cells are pending in the matrix the audit reads.** `CLI_ADAPTER_STRESS_MATRIX` is the seed table with `testStatus: pending` for every non-codex cell, but `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX` overlays `CLI_ADAPTER_PHASE_TWO_ROWS` and `CLI_ADAPTER_FANOUT_ROWS` on it, and the audit tests that overlay. `fanout.vitest.ts` asserts `allAdapterBound: true`, `allSubjectBound: true` and no forbidden overclaims, and that assertion is part of the gated suite. Reading the seed table alone would wrongly report 112 pending cells. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:132] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:147] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fanout.vitest.ts:359]\\n\\n3. **The matrix's bijection validator fails at HEAD with 126 of 126 tests \\\"missing\\\", because its parser cannot read the current `vitest list` output.** The validator spawns `npx --no-install vitest list tests/stress/cli-adapter --configLoader runner` and keeps only lines that start with `tests/stress/cli-adapter`, but the current output prefixes every line with the project name, for example `[serial] tests/stress/cli-adapter/cli-pi.vitest.ts > ...`. It discovers 0 tests and reports 126 missing, exit 1. The test bodies and the phase-two names exist; the parser is stale. Stripping an optional `[...] ` prefix would restore the bijection. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:100] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:116]\\n\\n4. **No workflow runs that validator, so its FAIL is invisible.** A search of `.github/workflows` finds the sk-doc `validate-playbook-package.cjs` in `playbook-operator-contract.yml`, but no invocation of the cli-adapter validator; the deep-loop workflow runs only the vitest suite. The manifest-integrity test checks the audit object, not the test-name bijection, so the two halves of the claim are separately gated and one half is not gated at all. [SOURCE: .github/workflows/playbook-operator-contract.yml:67] [SOURCE: .github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:86]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Is the cli-adapter stress suite part of a default test or CI gate? Yes: default `npm test` via the serial project, and the deep-loop CI workflow on the relevant paths. Finding 1.\\n- Which matrix cells remain pending at HEAD? None in `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX`; the seed table's pending cells are overlaid by implemented phase-two and fanout rows. Finding 2.\\n- Why does the matrix validator disagree? Finding 3: a stale parser, not missing tests. Finding 4: the validator is not wired into CI.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Whether the validator should be a vitest test in the gated suite or a workflow step; the test placement is cheaper to keep honest.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-2-008: whether any runner path reads `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and persists a provider session id for a `--only-lineage` rerun.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Treating `CLI_ADAPTER_STRESS_MATRIX` as the live matrix.** The overlay is the live object and the audit proves it; the seed table is documentation of the phase-one state.\\n- **Adding another CI workflow for the validator.** The existing deep-loop workflow already installs and runs the suite; one added step is enough.\\n- **Rewriting the validator to import the tests instead of listing them.** `vitest list` is the supported discovery surface; the parser, not the mechanism, is wrong.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Grepping workflows for `cli-adapter` or `validate-playbook-package`: only the sk-doc validator appears, which is a different path and a different package.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"pending at HEAD\\\" could mean the seed table or the audit view. Both are reported; the audit view is the one that gates.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the README says the validator \\\"proves that each row resolves to exactly one running test\\\"; the run shows 126 missing. The README describes the intent, the parser is stale. Recorded, not collapsed.\\n- Missing dependencies: none. `npx --no-install vitest` resolved locally.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/vitest.config.ts:14`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/package.json:1`\\n- `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:74`\\n- `.github/workflows/deep-loop-runtime.yml:86`\\n- `.github/workflows/playbook-operator-contract.yml:67`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:132`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/matrix-manifest.ts:147`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/fanout.vitest.ts:359`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:100`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/validate-playbook-package.cjs:116`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.75\\n- Questions addressed: gate wiring and pending-cell state.\\n- Questions answered: both.\\n- Finding mix: 2 fully new (the stale parser, the unwired validator) and 2 partially new confirmations (the serial-project gate, the overlay).\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: running the validator and then its underlying command separated \\\"the tests are missing\\\" from \\\"the parser is stale\\\" in two calls; the exit code alone would have been misleading.\\n- What did not work and why: reading the seed matrix first suggested 112 pending cells; only the overlay and the audit made the live state clear.\\n- What I would do differently: start from `CLI_ADAPTER_CURRENT_MATRIX` and the audit, then explain the seed table as history, rather than the reverse.\\n\\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\\n\\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795180117710,"end":1795180124329}}}}
