{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1795180183156,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"id":"prt_1f913be74001McQnufPymFAmd4","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f913b5c7001uIiO3o9HBt9Di8","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9f6c46563f2f8018c63d0f4bae60ab6f9b2e90fd"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795180189911,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f913be76001oUp237fQxVGPsB","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f913b5c7001uIiO3o9HBt9Di8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80568fd3d036e2cc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 6: F-2-008 session environment and rerun identity\n\n## Focus\n\nFrontier node F-2-008 (depth 2, scope runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts, runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs): Does any runner path read EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND and persist a provider session id for a --only-lineage rerun, or is it detection-only?\n\nThe node was read as: trace the constant to every reader, then trace what a `--only-lineage` rerun actually reuses.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and every reference to it in the runtime.\n2. Read `detectFromRuntimeEnv` and its caller in `validateExecutorDispatchAllowed`.\n3. Read `readStoredLineageSessionId` and `buildLineageDispatch`'s use of it.\n4. Grepped the fanout and dispatch scripts for any resume flag, provider session field or session-id extraction from a CLI log.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **`EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` is detection-only: its sole reader is the recursion guard.** `detectFromRuntimeEnv` returns true when the kind's session variable is set, and `validateExecutorDispatchAllowed` turns that into an `env`-layer refusal before spawn. Nothing writes the value to `effective_config`, the lineage config or the summary, and `fanout-run.cjs` never imports the constant. The table exists to stop a kind invoking itself, not to resume it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:85] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:903] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:1011]\n\n2. **The only rerun identity is the stored SPECKIT session id, and no adapter turns it into a provider-session resume.** `buildLineageDispatch` calls `readStoredLineageSessionId` and falls back to `fanout-<label>-<runId>`; the id is written into the prompt and the preview as `session_id`. No builder emits `--resume`, `--session`, `--continue` or a codex `exec resume` subcommand, and the runner does not parse a `session_id` out of a CLI log. A `--only-lineage` rerun therefore re-reads the lineage's artifacts and prompt but starts a fresh provider conversation. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:765] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3881] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3967]\n\n3. **The guard's env layer covers four of eight kinds by design, and no table says which layer covers the rest.** The map names codex, claude, opencode and cursor; pi and vibe are commented as unconfirmed and devin as absent, while dsh has no session env and is caught by its state-dir check instead. Self-invocation is still refused for the others by the stack, ancestry or lockfile layers, but the coverage is implicit in code rather than stated per kind. A guard-layer row beside the adapter capability record would make \"this kind cannot self-detect by env\" a declared fact instead of a comment. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:82] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:163]\n\n4. **The honest fix is to name artifact resume, and to capture a provider id only if model-session resume is actually wanted.** Today's behaviour is coherent: a rerun resumes the loop from `deep-research-state.jsonl` and the node store, which is what makes a retry cheap. Calling it \"session resume\" overstates it. If provider resume is wanted, the JSON shapes already carry an id (opencode's events and cursor's `--output-format json` both report one), so the runner can extract it, persist it in the lineage config under a `providerSession` key, and pass the adapter's resume flag on a rerun; until then, the capability record should say `resume: artifact-only` for every kind. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:90] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:37]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Does any runner path read `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and persist a provider session id? No. Finding 1: the only reader is the recursion guard; nothing persists the value.\n- Is it detection-only? Yes, and the rerun identity is artifact-based. Findings 1 and 2.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Whether model-session resume is worth building for the kinds whose logs report an id, or whether artifact resume is sufficient for the retry use case.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nNone: this was the last open frontier node for this lineage. Synthesis should now produce the ranked report and the frontier-drained stop.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Persisting the env value as the rerun identity.** The env is the parent's provider session, not the child's, and the recursion guard deliberately reads it to refuse dispatch; storing it would conflate the guard with resume.\n- **Adding resume flags to all eight adapters at once.** Four kinds report no session id in a parseable shape, and the two unconfirmed envs would need live probes; per-kind capture is the only honest path.\n- **Treating `session_id` in the preview as a provider id.** It is the SPECKIT session used for artifact scoping, as `buildLineageDispatch` shows.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Grepping for `--resume` or `exec resume` in `fanout-run.cjs` and `dispatch-iteration.cjs`: no match. The absence is the finding.\n- Looking for a log parser that extracts a session id: none exists; the only log parsers are cost and quota.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"session resume\" could mean artifact continuity or provider conversation continuity. Both readings are answered separately in Findings 1-4; the code implements the first.\n- Contradictory evidence: the adapter comments mention a \"session\" for cursor's env, but no builder consumes it. The comment is about detection, not resume.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:82`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:85`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:90`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:163`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:903`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:1011`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:765`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3881`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3967`\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:37`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.75\n- Questions addressed: the rerun identity question.\n- Questions answered: both parts.\n- Finding mix: 2 fully new traces (detection-only, artifact-only) and 2 partially new refinements (guard coverage, the naming/capture fix).\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: following the constant to its only caller settled \"detection-only\" in one grep; the absence of any resume flag in the builders settled the other half.\n- What did not work and why: the preview's `session_id` looked like a provider id for a moment; reading `buildLineageDispatch` showed it is the SPECKIT session, so the label is misleading rather than the mechanism.\n- What I would do differently: check the preview label against the builder before treating it as evidence, since the preview is where the ambiguity starts.\n\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\n","path":"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 6: F-2-008 session environment and rerun identity\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nFrontier node F-2-008 (depth 2, scope runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts, runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs): Does any runner path read EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND and persist a provider session id for a --only-lineage rerun, or is it detection-only?\\n\\nThe node was read as: trace the constant to every reader, then trace what a `--only-lineage` rerun actually reuses.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and every reference to it in the runtime.\\n2. Read `detectFromRuntimeEnv` and its caller in `validateExecutorDispatchAllowed`.\\n3. Read `readStoredLineageSessionId` and `buildLineageDispatch`'s use of it.\\n4. Grepped the fanout and dispatch scripts for any resume flag, provider session field or session-id extraction from a CLI log.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **`EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` is detection-only: its sole reader is the recursion guard.** `detectFromRuntimeEnv` returns true when the kind's session variable is set, and `validateExecutorDispatchAllowed` turns that into an `env`-layer refusal before spawn. Nothing writes the value to `effective_config`, the lineage config or the summary, and `fanout-run.cjs` never imports the constant. The table exists to stop a kind invoking itself, not to resume it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:85] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:903] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:1011]\\n\\n2. **The only rerun identity is the stored SPECKIT session id, and no adapter turns it into a provider-session resume.** `buildLineageDispatch` calls `readStoredLineageSessionId` and falls back to `fanout-<label>-<runId>`; the id is written into the prompt and the preview as `session_id`. No builder emits `--resume`, `--session`, `--continue` or a codex `exec resume` subcommand, and the runner does not parse a `session_id` out of a CLI log. A `--only-lineage` rerun therefore re-reads the lineage's artifacts and prompt but starts a fresh provider conversation. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:765] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3881] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3967]\\n\\n3. **The guard's env layer covers four of eight kinds by design, and no table says which layer covers the rest.** The map names codex, claude, opencode and cursor; pi and vibe are commented as unconfirmed and devin as absent, while dsh has no session env and is caught by its state-dir check instead. Self-invocation is still refused for the others by the stack, ancestry or lockfile layers, but the coverage is implicit in code rather than stated per kind. A guard-layer row beside the adapter capability record would make \\\"this kind cannot self-detect by env\\\" a declared fact instead of a comment. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:82] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:163]\\n\\n4. **The honest fix is to name artifact resume, and to capture a provider id only if model-session resume is actually wanted.** Today's behaviour is coherent: a rerun resumes the loop from `deep-research-state.jsonl` and the node store, which is what makes a retry cheap. Calling it \\\"session resume\\\" overstates it. If provider resume is wanted, the JSON shapes already carry an id (opencode's events and cursor's `--output-format json` both report one), so the runner can extract it, persist it in the lineage config under a `providerSession` key, and pass the adapter's resume flag on a rerun; until then, the capability record should say `resume: artifact-only` for every kind. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:90] [SOURCE: specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:37]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Does any runner path read `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` and persist a provider session id? No. Finding 1: the only reader is the recursion guard; nothing persists the value.\\n- Is it detection-only? Yes, and the rerun identity is artifact-based. Findings 1 and 2.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Whether model-session resume is worth building for the kinds whose logs report an id, or whether artifact resume is sufficient for the retry use case.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nNone: this was the last open frontier node for this lineage. Synthesis should now produce the ranked report and the frontier-drained stop.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Persisting the env value as the rerun identity.** The env is the parent's provider session, not the child's, and the recursion guard deliberately reads it to refuse dispatch; storing it would conflate the guard with resume.\\n- **Adding resume flags to all eight adapters at once.** Four kinds report no session id in a parseable shape, and the two unconfirmed envs would need live probes; per-kind capture is the only honest path.\\n- **Treating `session_id` in the preview as a provider id.** It is the SPECKIT session used for artifact scoping, as `buildLineageDispatch` shows.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Grepping for `--resume` or `exec resume` in `fanout-run.cjs` and `dispatch-iteration.cjs`: no match. The absence is the finding.\\n- Looking for a log parser that extracts a session id: none exists; the only log parsers are cost and quota.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"session resume\\\" could mean artifact continuity or provider conversation continuity. Both readings are answered separately in Findings 1-4; the code implements the first.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the adapter comments mention a \\\"session\\\" for cursor's env, but no builder consumes it. The comment is about detection, not resume.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: none.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:82`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:85`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:90`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:163`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:903`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:1011`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:765`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3881`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3967`\\n- `specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md:37`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.75\\n- Questions addressed: the rerun identity question.\\n- Questions answered: both parts.\\n- Finding mix: 2 fully new traces (detection-only, artifact-only) and 2 partially new refinements (guard coverage, the naming/capture fix).\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: following the constant to its only caller settled \\\"detection-only\\\" in one grep; the absence of any resume flag in the builders settled the other half.\\n- What did not work and why: the preview's `session_id` looked like a provider id for a moment; reading `buildLineageDispatch` showed it is the SPECKIT session, so the label is misleading rather than the mechanism.\\n- What I would do differently: check the preview label against the builder before treating it as evidence, since the preview is where the ambiguity starts.\\n\\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\\n\\nNone. No file outside the lineage directory was written.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1795180183158,"end":1795180189911}}}}
