{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1795180196780,"sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","part":{"partID":"prt_1f913f2d4002zhLzLioNbTi3hK","sessionID":"ses_e06f76d3effe0tIIpNFnvfaBvH","messageID":"msg_1f913eb9b001fF1CL1HURcjLW2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b91475c1b384e7a2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \"^\\*\\*.*Session resume\\|^5\\. \\*\\*\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md | head"},"output":"27:5. **\"Session resume\" is artifact resume only, and the code models it for half the kinds.** No builder forwards a resume or session flag: claude runs `-p`, codex runs `exec`, opencode runs `run --standalone`, and the four other builders do the same without a session argument. `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` names a session env for codex, claude, opencode and cursor and deliberately omits pi, vibe and dsh; `EXECUTOR_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` names a state dir for every kind. For dsh the gap is structural: one fresh `DSH_HOME` is created per attempt and removed when the attempt settles, so a retry cannot resume the previous attempt's harness state even if a resume flag existed. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:89] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:103] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4262] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4669]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"27:5. **\"Session resume\" is artifact resume only, and the code models it for half the kinds.** No builder forwards a resume or session flag: claude runs `-p`, codex runs `exec`, opencode runs `run --standalone`, and the four other builders do the same without a session argument. `EXECUTOR_SESSION_ENV_BY_KIND` names a session env for codex, claude, opencode and cursor and deliberately omits pi, vibe and dsh; `EXECUTOR_STATE_ENV_BY_KIND` names a state dir for every kind. For dsh the gap is structural: one fresh `DSH_HOME` is created per attempt and removed when the attempt settles, so a retry cannot resume the previous attempt's harness state even if a resume flag existed. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:89] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:103] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4262] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4669]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/455-expansive-depth-integration && grep -n \\\"^\\\\*\\\\*.*Session resume\\\\|^5\\\\. \\\\*\\\\*\\\" specs/system-deep-loop/loop-architecture/002-graph-engineering/007-expansive-depth-mode/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1795180196564,"end":1795180196780}}}}
